t/a2b7d8d14b18903daa0a64271db059a0f494254c","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/a2b7d8d14b18903daa0a64271db059a0f494254c/comments","author":{"login":"nick-hollon-lc","id":274035459,"node_id":"U_kgDOEFVzAw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/274035459?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/nick-hollon-lc","html_url":"https://github.com/nick-hollon-lc","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nick-hollon-lc/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nick-hollon-lc/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nick-hollon-lc/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nick-hollon-lc/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nick-hollon-lc/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nick-hollon-lc/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nick-hollon-lc/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nick-hollon-lc/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nick-hollon-lc/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"aab9ca62c38ea359dfde3cf7b44897e651a0f63f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/aab9ca62c38ea359dfde3cf7b44897e651a0f63f","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/aab9ca62c38ea359dfde3cf7b44897e651a0f63f"}]},{"sha":"aab9ca62c38ea359dfde3cf7b44897e651a0f63f","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKGFhYjljYTYyYzM4ZWEzNTlkZmRlM2NmN2I0NDg5N2U2NTFhMGY2M2Y","commit":{"author":{"name":"Nick Hollon","email":"nick.hollon@langchain.dev","date":"2026-07-01T00:33:20Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-07-01T00:33:20Z"},"message":"feat(evals): harbor workflow stress-test inputs + sharding (#4381)\n\n- **`agent_timeout_multiplier`** — scale the agent EXECUTION timeout\n(e.g. `0.1` to bound per-rollout wall-clock for cheap concurrency stress\ntests; setup/env-build budgets unaffected).\n- **`disable_verification`** — skip the task verifier (tests) for\nsetup/concurrency stress runs.\n- **`n_shards`** — split the dataset's tasks across N parallel shard\njobs per model\n- **`--reinstall --refresh`** on the `harbor_package_override` install,\nso re-running the same git ref picks up a freshly-built wheel instead of\na stale cached one\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Mason Daugherty <github@mdrxy.com>","tree":{"sha":"7c73614c767fd07bff4e5b623a817a92885b61fb","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/7c73614c767fd07bff4e5b623a817a92885b61fb"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/aab9ca62c38ea359dfde3cf7b44897e651a0f63f","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqRGBQCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAaY8QAGPwlnYlf6qU6iH3UYx8rZIe\nz7vqhXcCe2uMipP/hu2lF8XF0qh/vooUc/7M7mUj9qSgXv83lScA5Itym9rmDDD6\ny5yuVH0FPIJNyYXt97M6uuIaHE4dZp0FLFbD6RbYz0EbYygQ1eLOmeWQpP2ozD9R\n5GjKkK3hHvCZKIkpOgCm558cZJJY/y3wF9XpYdGyOyvDHWVP6pBc0PGH2uW1PnG7\n7zrz6fdCmxub6LDiMLs3+ksf3jkfgs6qUgoi2VwxRtkZw6UlxOyZjEAWBwPnS292\noFUteJUBSSvVNAwkm2lb92n93C+FgzplQvIaD3uf7j8U91K4ktaW6OI2AOVJRo+f\n2g/7SSMe/trQbk1ZW3ARixuwqEmjMYCqnmzJeZTf2DNgauR/o+RDj7tC5MpT4Wrn\nv8/cdPsDxaHyGp1ZeKdW5csE2DkmOI49Jj3GCZLwbXBsrDDq2SA5hc3iq2QqPg69\nAN0P/mssPvlj41tZ/FmxxKIGxiZpoEYxeZ/4rknKIXM0OMH+v1cBfKp8h+mOBbBL\nty+AjnIfRXbwBOofm1Mwo2X5jjG5q1ha3PqymRm9O/Lbc3sd2Eq8sH9uk09N5QEM\nysFFJM85gvAY6DlsR0jh39J9p+kYd5hrOGNPnU7v4VujzbhVkDWdQ10FmPKqIM+h\nb8amtaWHZQS6G9xNXeEh\n=2DNd\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 7c73614c767fd07bff4e5b623a817a92885b61fb\nparent 8b7eab023db686f577d16f4f9ac872205baf136f\nauthor Nick Hollon <nick.hollon@langchain.dev> 1782866000 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1782866000 -0400\n\nfeat(evals): harbor workflow stress-test inputs + sharding (#4381)\n\n- **`agent_timeout_multiplier`** — scale the agent EXECUTION timeout\n(e.g. `0.1` to bound per-rollout wall-clock for cheap concurrency stress\ntests; setup/env-build budgets unaffected).\n- **`disable_verification`** — skip the task verifier (tests) for\nsetup/concurrency stress runs.\n- **`n_shards`** — split the dataset's tasks across N parallel shard\njobs per model\n- **`--reinstall --refresh`** on the `harbor_package_override` install,\nso re-running the same git ref picks up a freshly-built wheel instead of\na stale cached one\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Mason Daugherty <github@mdrxy.com>","verified_at":"2026-07-01T00:33:20Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/aab9ca62c38ea359dfde3cf7b44897e651a0f63f","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/aab9ca62c38ea359dfde3cf7b44897e651a0f63f","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/aab9ca62c38ea359dfde3cf7b44897e651a0f63f/comments","author":{"login":"nick-hollon-lc","id":274035459,"node_id":"U_kgDOEFVzAw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/274035459?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/nick-hollon-lc","html_url":"https://github.com/nick-hollon-lc","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nick-hollon-lc/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nick-hollon-lc/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nick-hollon-lc/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nick-hollon-lc/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nick-hollon-lc/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nick-hollon-lc/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nick-hollon-lc/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nick-hollon-lc/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nick-hollon-lc/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"8b7eab023db686f577d16f4f9ac872205baf136f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/8b7eab023db686f577d16f4f9ac872205baf136f","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/8b7eab023db686f577d16f4f9ac872205baf136f"}]},{"sha":"8b7eab023db686f577d16f4f9ac872205baf136f","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKDhiN2VhYjAyM2RiNjg2ZjU3N2QxNmY0ZjlhYzg3MjIwNWJhZjEzNmY","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-06-30T21:51:46Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-30T21:51:46Z"},"message":"fix(code): unblock MCP force reconnect modal (#4396)\n\nFixed `/mcp reconnect force` so its confirmation modal no longer traps\nthe TUI; Enter confirms, Esc cancels, and the app remains responsive.\n\n---\n\nThe MCP force-reconnect confirmation now returns control to Textual's\nevent loop instead of awaiting the modal from the chat-input submit\nhandler. That lets Enter, Esc, and quit shortcuts work while the modal\nis open, and still runs the reconnect only after explicit confirmation.\n\n## Changes\n- Replace the blocking `_push_screen_wait` call in\n`_handle_mcp_reconnect_command(force=True)` with callback-style\n`push_screen`, so the force-confirm modal can receive follow-up key\nevents.\n- Schedule `_restart_server_for_mcp_refresh(\"forced reconnect\")` from\nthe confirmation callback and attach `_log_task_exception` so detached\nrestart failures are still surfaced.\n- Treat cancel and programmatic dismiss as safe no-ops that return focus\nto the chat input, and notify if the confirmation modal cannot be\nmounted.\n- Cover the real modal path with pilot-driven tests for Enter, Esc/focus\nrestoration, mount failure, and the pending-reconnect bypass.","tree":{"sha":"d2a9f3e3c554f659f1b7d8cd8943a1e32d3ceaa0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/d2a9f3e3c554f659f1b7d8cd8943a1e32d3ceaa0"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/8b7eab023db686f577d16f4f9ac872205baf136f","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqRDpyCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAt6MQABO7nvtzFUxUn6cWkLUWexdB\nQnfswUmZLBKj/a9MhUgmhOdlpMJneUVU/bwvQZJzJ7RSBpKWdh+ivHQqwyNub0qz\nSlQSRDgXhHNTWPcV9PUNUig0opK0sJA8NHM/PY+0N3xkoBlakKjgRf/INmbMcDl3\nVTCPuT8RO5tM9wT4TEB7k4CMuA6YrXY9mQcM94ksz4QDuZSET91IhwAkF/6MEQ0t\nqKh6xAbQa445SGCxj1A7B95NggaHJ+O1XODd6qGlDhM/+1qtcIN/b0bG/hAytVEQ\n2Xiugw9NRdFsMfsdZ0QEt1+Eyf3VzSPOgt5WBFj+ub14xSYI0usvemqj2ZIizLxX\nwmsPl48YVkmWxPKeXOyaMj66MfHj+3cdXJbihFv4acH+Hz+rOqHEadZKLOhmQY6S\nvdEOpCtqK1ACWkHEsdFDwL43krBcqoKImpgPqM8NF+WjYawhhCk3wmOc6gtRdJEG\n82Z1UHvehD3wzm/w2UZ/sOVio9NcgSPvyv4sKFfw74Zvp88YUeHRUFO0PTSVeh67\nnasmmLfjRlXH9gUBeHROrZxDRrz8lxlizgpWtICHqbSVoYipS2xQByqOUxclI+sa\nRZ9bX7zoDqfg2o1ZHPkK5OPZUL2nQW0xnZulSCzLq7+ujnv9VXVjHWnhpj6io/wI\nQzAN2RBkFseGU891DLwP\n=4YJl\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree d2a9f3e3c554f659f1b7d8cd8943a1e32d3ceaa0\nparent 3239bf4edf2be3037bb18315463ac6a0c3537e5c\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1782856306 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1782856306 -0400\n\nfix(code): unblock MCP force reconnect modal (#4396)\n\nFixed `/mcp reconnect force` so its confirmation modal no longer traps\nthe TUI; Enter confirms, Esc cancels, and the app remains responsive.\n\n---\n\nThe MCP force-reconnect confirmation now returns control to Textual's\nevent loop instead of awaiting the modal from the chat-input submit\nhandler. That lets Enter, Esc, and quit shortcuts work while the modal\nis open, and still runs the reconnect only after explicit confirmation.\n\n## Changes\n- Replace the blocking `_push_screen_wait` call in\n`_handle_mcp_reconnect_command(force=True)` with callback-style\n`push_screen`, so the force-confirm modal can receive follow-up key\nevents.\n- Schedule `_restart_server_for_mcp_refresh(\"forced reconnect\")` from\nthe confirmation callback and attach `_log_task_exception` so detached\nrestart failures are still surfaced.\n- Treat cancel and programmatic dismiss as safe no-ops that return focus\nto the chat input, and notify if the confirmation modal cannot be\nmounted.\n- Cover the real modal path with pilot-driven tests for Enter, Esc/focus\nrestoration, mount failure, and the pending-reconnect bypass.","verified_at":"2026-06-30T21:51:47Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/8b7eab023db686f577d16f4f9ac872205baf136f","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/8b7eab023db686f577d16f4f9ac872205baf136f","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/8b7eab023db686f577d16f4f9ac872205baf136f/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"3239bf4edf2be3037bb18315463ac6a0c3537e5c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/3239bf4edf2be3037bb18315463ac6a0c3537e5c","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/3239bf4edf2be3037bb18315463ac6a0c3537e5c"}]},{"sha":"3239bf4edf2be3037bb18315463ac6a0c3537e5c","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKDMyMzliZjRlZGYyYmUzMDM3YmIxODMxNTQ2M2FjNmEwYzM1MzdlNWM","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-06-30T20:54:16Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-30T20:54:16Z"},"message":"fix(code): resolve editable SDK version metadata (#4394)\n\nEditable installs now report dcode and SDK version metadata from the\nsame resolver used elsewhere, so diagnostics reflect the checked-out\nsource instead of stale package metadata. The stream config still keeps\nthe heavier resolver off the module import path and treats SDK version\nreporting as best-effort metadata.","tree":{"sha":"ac52fff8b2ec1f5c84f6f9f8231097f7b8768217","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/ac52fff8b2ec1f5c84f6f9f8231097f7b8768217"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/3239bf4edf2be3037bb18315463ac6a0c3537e5c","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqRCz4CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAQa4QALCwEuSZbBk3FvOwtZQdYgfI\nX9nqsyqyeHNR0umnCUgXwKhOwj8K1Rs5GVbJqDOO/L1FOyGUGZNWw/furZiSd0zP\ng5ogrb+NO3sWyOgNBjpC8ChWMLUB57z1vaFC2yYxhSHmfBP2rbo3PhArG3cVOOfJ\nRId9JEwZfXeNEFF64vJ0LXJz9aEBGcaaW31dCPrH2sNetfVqVRuS4moGlMkpa8Ch\nc99eA0FHcbWqu4J2ZT+8Cu796JnHjSXeI++J8cS/Wqfn5syDUI3YGNgWmzy4nBei\nXkUg+swG1sfb0RiBQx6+eXuf+Y2ynCALNRpRkEgGgYm0zoPQZpzUocVhplPmiX+N\n0IQRNA9bQ7bBkPUgjcwXZDljT7DRKIplk9qT0MBcWScEZsBbZRynvbHnd9GiJmgy\nucrSJR648qGQQUAbekTrnIEo/2DI4zw7yZUIcfykNmdjhdtsRUd3AXXfeG6VGG6j\n5U1cajd+P7/86KCxwhX6NgTZqdWOPfk4wjpK3k8apvme6GRYzSWvkSc/OttmgT4q\nZ6kp8EVDqrfKP1Ss78Bz/cI87l6r1ChGqeoGf/9/KaYP1SHreszDFOocAax53KGx\nmdy9Gqi9hq0m3B6fsUbMjDAtu+cY4fA00IF+7rqeDErAuXImtSAsAuw25cbXy8Lf\nbrzi2eVZCIAiGSMExey1\n=FlIz\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree ac52fff8b2ec1f5c84f6f9f8231097f7b8768217\nparent 1f8e8dc942ac54c4014ac48f9345ee0201be0b1b\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1782852856 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1782852856 -0400\n\nfix(code): resolve editable SDK version metadata (#4394)\n\nEditable installs now report dcode and SDK version metadata from the\nsame resolver used elsewhere, so diagnostics reflect the checked-out\nsource instead of stale package metadata. The stream config still keeps\nthe heavier resolver off the module import path and treats SDK version\nreporting as best-effort metadata.","verified_at":"2026-06-30T20:54:17Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/3239bf4edf2be3037bb18315463ac6a0c3537e5c","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/3239bf4edf2be3037bb18315463ac6a0c3537e5c","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/3239bf4edf2be3037bb18315463ac6a0c3537e5c/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"1f8e8dc942ac54c4014ac48f9345ee0201be0b1b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/1f8e8dc942ac54c4014ac48f9345ee0201be0b1b","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/1f8e8dc942ac54c4014ac48f9345ee0201be0b1b"}]},{"sha":"1f8e8dc942ac54c4014ac48f9345ee0201be0b1b","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKDFmOGU4ZGM5NDJhYzU0YzQwMTRhYzQ4ZjkzNDVlZTAyMDFiZTBiMWI","commit":{"author":{"name":"Johannes du Plessis","email":"johannes@langchain.dev","date":"2026-06-30T20:47:02Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-30T20:47:02Z"},"message":"fix(code): full-width chat messages, hide scrollbar, flush input bg (#4374)\n\nCloses #3548\n\n---\n\nThe chat surface had two nits: message blocks didn't line up with the\ninput box (the chat container had horizontal padding the input border\ndidn't), and the vertical scrollbar was always on unless the terminal\nwas in ASCII mode — with no way for a user to hide it on a capable\nterminal.\n\nThis makes the chat area flush with the input box and adds a\nuser-toggleable scrollbar so people can choose whether the scrollbar is\nvisible.\n\n- `#chat` drops its horizontal padding so message blocks span the same\nfull width as the input box border below.\n- The input box and status bar switch from `$surface` to `$background`\nso they blend with the app background instead of reading as a separate\nband.\n- New `/scrollbar` slash command toggles the vertical scrollbar on or\noff for the current session and persists the choice to\n`[ui].show_scrollbar` (and `DEEPAGENTS_CODE_SHOW_SCROLLBAR` for an\nenv-var override). It defaults to off, matching the look of other coding\nCLIs; wheel and keyboard scrolling still work when the scrollbar is\nhidden. ASCII-mode terminals keep the scrollbar hidden regardless of the\npreference, since they can't render the glyphs.\n\n## Screenshots\n### Before\n<img width=\"861\" height=\"632\" alt=\"Screenshot 2026-06-29 at 5 38 10 PM\"\nsrc=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/4add48dd-f761-4edf-a2a1-aefa9c6e4697\"\n/>\n\n### After\n<img width=\"862\" height=\"634\" alt=\"Screenshot 2026-06-29 at 5 36 48 PM\"\nsrc=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/d7ecb5b7-87b3-4122-8b28-bc61b248b670\"\n/>\n<img width=\"857\" height=\"634\" alt=\"Screenshot 2026-06-29 at 5 37 19 PM\"\nsrc=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/2f656c5b-5509-4326-a68a-ad2a3a59fd6a\"\n/>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Mason Daugherty <github@mdrxy.com>\nCo-authored-by: Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev>","tree":{"sha":"6187a16f3c462ff67d50a65124d8eebfda615a38","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/6187a16f3c462ff67d50a65124d8eebfda615a38"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/1f8e8dc942ac54c4014ac48f9345ee0201be0b1b","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqRCtGCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAjOQQAGjyT8n9o9Zr+aWNscCicPvI\nVsD7nNcV/dxVgadW8hFXalzY7QiPuYNusgNEQd3/bDxEPBlFNJc5Zmg2uCRHzR60\nzejXExJdb9uXVPNGWJK1PW4aqSnn+lDCUeMI05qbu8oyeFSH+Ia7eVg2y9qivFeZ\nNoViwb+mrsSuWol1/a2rzJ08MSCgbe+gNCRc1sf67HlLtZecy57zUjZCNNdU9yY/\n4Row6NTiy0po34lEUJbeh5U4nxCFvYHFrRntV0dfn4nvw+3XrKs0f1c3HnWl67c+\niACwf5OMw9rVBdW8EvkiVp3VIdb2QGrshyen1meeq7AO46FFIDm9pGJLSNvUKgxx\n2T205rYW3ObbW1r0+Wry8xVT1JnNF+JZ6rJizSNqOzkJwmtByJZ2vWPnDgAKehLN\ner7xcXELur6bUYP8Pc6+FXfiUumvqaDvGpn9CXUGn17enekoF91Y69itWLjZ4tRz\ntcmtmy+s7bWPajbUaa4aFJ9BRi4CllG0S1CsGgJpKU8/yjWFfHXpiNy7DDwOOZhA\nQ367J+0Aulf2N6RAI+7aIZvu89JkD2Ty4uBH2Rcppm6eMoPf5si9TopzquHajzFa\n4ba751XHEeouwc/6ei8v3MXtyEj/DvO+BaoxgYcvs+I5EKcriS/pgUxLIQBFJHZ1\ntvB9vCTVDtP5urTmaSgB\n=3HuP\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 6187a16f3c462ff67d50a65124d8eebfda615a38\nparent 83898ba608b29fc1bd1e9b4118b5e89a99c40f21\nauthor Johannes du Plessis <johannes@langchain.dev> 1782852422 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1782852422 -0400\n\nfix(code): full-width chat messages, hide scrollbar, flush input bg (#4374)\n\nCloses #3548\n\n---\n\nThe chat surface had two nits: message blocks didn't line up with the\ninput box (the chat container had horizontal padding the input border\ndidn't), and the vertical scrollbar was always on unless the terminal\nwas in ASCII mode — with no way for a user to hide it on a capable\nterminal.\n\nThis makes the chat area flush with the input box and adds a\nuser-toggleable scrollbar so people can choose whether the scrollbar is\nvisible.\n\n- `#chat` drops its horizontal padding so message blocks span the same\nfull width as the input box border below.\n- The input box and status bar switch from `$surface` to `$background`\nso they blend with the app background instead of reading as a separate\nband.\n- New `/scrollbar` slash command toggles the vertical scrollbar on or\noff for the current session and persists the choice to\n`[ui].show_scrollbar` (and `DEEPAGENTS_CODE_SHOW_SCROLLBAR` for an\nenv-var override). It defaults to off, matching the look of other coding\nCLIs; wheel and keyboard scrolling still work when the scrollbar is\nhidden. ASCII-mode terminals keep the scrollbar hidden regardless of the\npreference, since they can't render the glyphs.\n\n## Screenshots\n### Before\n<img width=\"861\" height=\"632\" alt=\"Screenshot 2026-06-29 at 5 38 10 PM\"\nsrc=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/4add48dd-f761-4edf-a2a1-aefa9c6e4697\"\n/>\n\n### After\n<img width=\"862\" height=\"634\" alt=\"Screenshot 2026-06-29 at 5 36 48 PM\"\nsrc=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/d7ecb5b7-87b3-4122-8b28-bc61b248b670\"\n/>\n<img width=\"857\" height=\"634\" alt=\"Screenshot 2026-06-29 at 5 37 19 PM\"\nsrc=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/2f656c5b-5509-4326-a68a-ad2a3a59fd6a\"\n/>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Mason Daugherty <github@mdrxy.com>\nCo-authored-by: Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev>","verified_at":"2026-06-30T20:47:03Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/1f8e8dc942ac54c4014ac48f9345ee0201be0b1b","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/1f8e8dc942ac54c4014ac48f9345ee0201be0b1b","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/1f8e8dc942ac54c4014ac48f9345ee0201be0b1b/comments","author":{"login":"johannes117","id":51395795,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUxMzk1Nzk1","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/51395795?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/us