))\n* Adopt coding-agent-v1 trace metadata\n([#4367](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/4367))\n([cb39747](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/cb3974748024fcec2e2ee0ccc0a9b23c880733a2))\n* Quit shortcut on completed update modal\n([#4312](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/4312))\n([5e6eae9](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/5e6eae9f094a5167b6bf01f2d84cf06ca5cd80c3))\n\n### Bug Fixes\n\n* Redact LangSmith trace secrets by default\n([#4356](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/4356))\n([5e01fec](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/5e01fec72d8b179a3b075b07268162d2eaebfe84))\n* Honor Baseten base URL env precedence\n([#4328](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/4328))\n([8f20d74](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/8f20d74892112c3b88aaca63d8c04a355fd6726f))\n* Highlight just-installed provider on `/auth` reopen\n([#4311](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/4311))\n([85e47b5](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/85e47b532b5caf92a52f1a070a95bdb39bee6d3d))\n* Clear transient update launch status\n([#4355](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/4355))\n([b870b18](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/b870b18750f65442009028a85a2ac18f1b06640c))\n* Clearer MCP config JSON parse errors\n([#4327](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/4327))\n([9cee602](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/9cee60274d38d4ad8a2d7a7e9d3ae59aebce5261))\n* Record shell output as user context\n([#4353](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/4353))\n([0d504a5](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/0d504a5df8454e871597932ce1cd3e95b10ab00e))\n* Suppress expected MCP reauth logs\n([#4359](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/4359))\n([15ee384](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/15ee384117ccd955f7481346dd92b7f4b007a60d))\n\n### Performance Improvements\n\n* Background refresh for `@` file completion cache\n([#3911](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/3911))\n([aa22d6b](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/aa22d6b6d5a49e4d6c3aa2d4932df75d14d65f78))\n* Speed up shutdown after `Ctrl+C`/`Ctrl+D`\n([#4351](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/4351))\n([db441ed](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/db441ed306a8e03fb68f2ae6a2c08523e248976d))\n\n---\n\n_Everything above this line will be the GitHub release body._\n\n---\n\n> [!NOTE]\n> A **New Contributors** section is appended to the GitHub release notes\nautomatically at publish time (see [Release\nPipeline](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/blob/main/.github/RELEASING.md#release-pipeline),\nstep 2).\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: github-actions[bot] <41898282+github-actions[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Mason Daugherty <github@mdrxy.com>","verified_at":"2026-06-29T20:55:34Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/14a0fb119e4db8bf48743ece164cce44d334a56a","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/14a0fb119e4db8bf48743ece164cce44d334a56a","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/14a0fb119e4db8bf48743ece164cce44d334a56a/comments","author":{"login":"github-actions[bot]","id":41898282,"node_id":"MDM6Qm90NDE4OTgyODI=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/15368?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/github-actions","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"cb3974748024fcec2e2ee0ccc0a9b23c880733a2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/cb3974748024fcec2e2ee0ccc0a9b23c880733a2","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/cb3974748024fcec2e2ee0ccc0a9b23c880733a2"}]},{"sha":"cb3974748024fcec2e2ee0ccc0a9b23c880733a2","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKGNiMzk3NDc0ODAyNGZjZWMyZTJlZTBjY2MwYTliMjNjODgwNzMzYTI","commit":{"author":{"name":"Hari Harish","email":"123656547+harisaiharish@users.noreply.github.com","date":"2026-06-29T20:41:01Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-29T20:41:01Z"},"message":"feat(code): adopt coding-agent-v1 trace metadata (#4367)\n\n**Why this is needed**\nLangSmith groups and filters coding-agent traces by a standard set of\nmetadata keys — the agent, its version, the conversation turn, and the\nrepo it ran in. Deep Agents Code didn't emit them, so its traces were\nthe odd one out: you\ncouldn't line them up against the other coding agents in dashboards or\nevals.\n\n**What this does**\nDeep Agents Code now stamps the shared coding-agent-v1 metadata contract\non its LangSmith traces, using the same stable keys as the other\nintegrations. Each trace now reliably records what agent and version\nproduced it, which user turn it belongs to, and the repo/git/cwd it ran\nin.\n\n**Changes (all in `libs/code`)**\n- New `_git.py`: resolves the commit SHA, remote URL, and parsed repo\nmetadata (provider/name).\n- `config.py`: a single `build_coding_agent_metadata()` helper wired\ninto `build_stream_config`; mirrors `thread_id` to top-level metadata\nand keeps existing keys.\n- Turn markers (`turn_id` + 1-based `turn_number`) tracked on session\nstate and passed through the interactive and non-interactive paths.\n- Tests for the git helpers, turn markers, and a contract test\nvalidating the metadata block against the vendored coding-agent-v1\nvalidator.\n\n**Known limitation**\nOn `chat_model` / `create_agent` runs, LangChain core overwrites\n`ls_integration` with its own value, so per-run `ls_integration` isn't\n`deepagents-code` there. Traces stay identifiable via\n`ls_agent_kind=\"coding_agent\"` and root-level `ls_integration`.\n\n**How I verified**\nVerified on a [live\ntrace](https://smith.langchain.com/o/ebbaf2eb-769b-4505-aca2-d11de10372a4/projects/p/32d59ccd-86a1-447c-8a6d-53ee4f75ce62?timeModel=%7B%22duration%22%3A%2230d%22%7D&peek=20260623T212320Z019ef65d-bf93-7450-9690-e0e4c72e09d0&peekedConversationId=019ef65c-5012-7521-a536-725278301be0&trace_id=019ef65d-bf93-7450-9690-e0e4c72e09d0&run_id=20260623T212320Z019ef65d-bf93-7450-9690-e0e4c72e09d0&peeked_trace=20260623T212320288794Z019ef65d-bf93-7450-9690-e0e4c72e09d0&conversationTab=trace&scroll_to=feedback)\n— all required keys present per run type.\n\n---\n\nFixes LSEN-307\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Mason Daugherty <github@mdrxy.com>\nCo-authored-by: Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev>","tree":{"sha":"3aa8c465ca6b3458cce9c17c5a50640de556a0ad","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/3aa8c465ca6b3458cce9c17c5a50640de556a0ad"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/cb3974748024fcec2e2ee0ccc0a9b23c880733a2","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqQthdCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAOMEQAFGyCklrXzXnky66HMO/6WPn\n6AF+F++8/KoRqE0HzdOmtV+0/8ug+GY+5J/29csV6LeicrJulqkQAV3D5jftMCBy\nz/NvVNtuQ6S28vm8o4fm4iRwlaiZyV7hgZLukMfyNPCC/c5qVHDWGGKxkWBxnXI3\n/uVywJNUJSXp3Prd5WY1z2uB0LiClxOVoPnOwArbd/Nb5ORoSZTU4Wn5GMLyMAwa\nobFRFgrTJvxkfOqmYZaVP9Zp8ZNpg2W4lXr5zPY5wxP/MWfRo+cFWu7c425UlpOz\nnI+csLvxSxJdjhwLx2xmcCDomdADDvzovgQxhvDTD1KPptfgWhILPwy4e7+Oeall\nKVMolXwi8l5sIh6TNypHQHBMclgumGIXiBvjBfw9eDo59rt3aTHnj7nVGtHqWyst\n/tkcGgStqbEThidsyucGBcNcqFB0kNS5MNdeLYIwtDaIe2VZTH9alqwZ4CoXKLar\n2BBxrBL95lvqROzlFeuSRBzRRj/ikD1/opM2ov/Yz6+WOLcicZG420EKvOvwxjZi\nGuixGeniDM8CO4iVLJ7RTfloi4r2iKq5T8MJW0L01WFAC+1Ncb78gTH/S/WiMUBF\n3XIkltIUbZWnOduuTPI25LK00cTmFuXezO61lV/YDb8nvfvCmVrvVCY0UG0o1dcX\nL5MvK/HkshmOhV6vcxuv\n=vub9\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 3aa8c465ca6b3458cce9c17c5a50640de556a0ad\nparent 8fca61dc036888a4414ff5a4536b957c63dab4a5\nauthor Hari Harish <123656547+harisaiharish@users.noreply.github.com> 1782765661 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1782765661 -0400\n\nfeat(code): adopt coding-agent-v1 trace metadata (#4367)\n\n**Why this is needed**\nLangSmith groups and filters coding-agent traces by a standard set of\nmetadata keys — the agent, its version, the conversation turn, and the\nrepo it ran in. Deep Agents Code didn't emit them, so its traces were\nthe odd one out: you\ncouldn't line them up against the other coding agents in dashboards or\nevals.\n\n**What this does**\nDeep Agents Code now stamps the shared coding-agent-v1 metadata contract\non its LangSmith traces, using the same stable keys as the other\nintegrations. Each trace now reliably records what agent and version\nproduced it, which user turn it belongs to, and the repo/git/cwd it ran\nin.\n\n**Changes (all in `libs/code`)**\n- New `_git.py`: resolves the commit SHA, remote URL, and parsed repo\nmetadata (provider/name).\n- `config.py`: a single `build_coding_agent_metadata()` helper wired\ninto `build_stream_config`; mirrors `thread_id` to top-level metadata\nand keeps existing keys.\n- Turn markers (`turn_id` + 1-based `turn_number`) tracked on session\nstate and passed through the interactive and non-interactive paths.\n- Tests for the git helpers, turn markers, and a contract test\nvalidating the metadata block against the vendored coding-agent-v1\nvalidator.\n\n**Known limitation**\nOn `chat_model` / `create_agent` runs, LangChain core overwrites\n`ls_integration` with its own value, so per-run `ls_integration` isn't\n`deepagents-code` there. Traces stay identifiable via\n`ls_agent_kind=\"coding_agent\"` and root-level `ls_integration`.\n\n**How I verified**\nVerified on a [live\ntrace](https://smith.langchain.com/o/ebbaf2eb-769b-4505-aca2-d11de10372a4/projects/p/32d59ccd-86a1-447c-8a6d-53ee4f75ce62?timeModel=%7B%22duration%22%3A%2230d%22%7D&peek=20260623T212320Z019ef65d-bf93-7450-9690-e0e4c72e09d0&peekedConversationId=019ef65c-5012-7521-a536-725278301be0&trace_id=019ef65d-bf93-7450-9690-e0e4c72e09d0&run_id=20260623T212320Z019ef65d-bf93-7450-9690-e0e4c72e09d0&peeked_trace=20260623T212320288794Z019ef65d-bf93-7450-9690-e0e4c72e09d0&conversationTab=trace&scroll_to=feedback)\n— all required keys present per run type.\n\n---\n\nFixes LSEN-307\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Mason Daugherty <github@mdrxy.com>\nCo-authored-by: Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev>","verified_at":"2026-06-29T20:41:01Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/cb3974748024fcec2e2ee0ccc0a9b23c880733a2","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/cb3974748024fcec2e2ee0ccc0a9b23c880733a2","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/cb3974748024fcec2e2ee0ccc0a9b23c880733a2/comments","author":{"login":"harisaiharish","id":123656547,"node_id":"U_kgDOB17ZYw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/123656547?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/harisaiharish","html_url":"https://github.com/harisaiharish","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/harisaiharish/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/harisaiharish/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/harisaiharish/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/harisaiharish/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/harisaiharish/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/harisaiharish/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/harisaiharish/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/harisaiharish/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/harisaiharish/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"8fca61dc036888a4414ff5a4536b957c63dab4a5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/8fca61dc036888a4414ff5a4536b957c63dab4a5","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/8fca61dc036888a4414ff5a4536b957c63dab4a5"}]},{"sha":"8fca61dc036888a4414ff5a4536b957c63dab4a5","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKDhmY2E2MWRjMDM2ODg4YTQ0MTRmZjVhNDUzNmI5NTdjNjNkYWI0YTU","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-06-29T20:20:18Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-29T20:20:18Z"},"message":"feat(code): add rubric-backed goal workflow (#4365)\n\nAdds rubric-driven acceptance criteria to Deep Agents Code and layers a\ngoal workflow on top of it.\n\nA rubric is the explicit definition of done. Use it when you already\nknow the criteria the agent should satisfy before it considers the work\ncomplete. Criteria can be sticky for the thread, one-shot for the next\nturn, or loaded from a file. While the agent works, the TUI shows\ngrading lifecycle messages so the user can see when the work is being\nchecked, revised, satisfied, or stopped.\n\nUsage examples:\n\n```text\n/rubric set tests pass; no unrelated files changed; help text is updated\n/rubric next only change the auth callback; do not refactor unrelated code\n/rubric file acceptance.md\n/rubric show\n/rubric clear\n```\n\nA goal is the objective-oriented workflow. Use it when you know the\noutcome, but want `dcode` to propose acceptance criteria before\nexecution. `/goal <objective>` asks the model to draft criteria and\ndisplays them in an inline review prompt. The user can accept the\ncriteria, edit them directly, reject them with feedback to regenerate,\nor cancel. Accepted goal criteria become the sticky rubric for the\nthread.\n\nUsage examples:\n\n```text\n/goal add OAuth refresh handling\n/goal show\n/goal clear\n```\n\nThe `--goal` CLI flag starts the same goal-review workflow when\nlaunching the TUI. It is intentionally interactive: the generated\ncriteria must be reviewed before execution. After the user accepts the\nproposal, the accepted goal is sent as the first task.\n\n```bash\ndcode --goal \"add OAuth refresh handling\"\n```\n\n`--goal` cannot be combined with `-n`, `-m`, `--skill`, or `--rubric`.\nFor non-interactive/headless runs, users should provide criteria\nexplicitly with `--rubric` instead:\n\n```bash\ndcode -n \"implement OAuth refresh handling\" --rubric \"tests pass; no unrelated files changed\"\ndcode -n \"implement OAuth refresh handling\" --rubric @acceptance.md\n```\n\nAccepted goal/rubric state is persisted on the thread and restored on\nresume. For example, a user can set `/goal add OAuth refresh handling`,\naccept the proposed criteria, quit the TUI, and later resume the same\nthread with the goal and criteria still active. That matters because the\nacceptance criteria continue to guide future turns and remain visible in\n`/goal show` instead of becoming hidden context that disappears between\nsessions.\n\nWhen the agent believes the goal is done, it does not get to declare\nvictory on its own. For example, after implementing OAuth refresh\nhandling, the agent can ask to mark the goal complete with evidence such\nas \"tests pass.\" `dcode` keeps that request pending until the rubric\ncheck finishes. If the rubric still needs revision, the goal stays\nactive and the user sees why it was not completed. If the rubric is\nsatisfied, auto-approve mode records the completion automatically;\nmanual mode asks the user before changing the goal status. This keeps\nthe user's accepted criteria as the source of truth for whether the goal\nis actually finished.\n\nThe active criteria and goal are also visible to the agent through\nconstrained tools. `get_rubric` lets the agent inspect the current\ncriteria and whether they came from a goal, a sticky rubric, or the\ncurrent invocation. `get_goal` lets it inspect the active objective,\nstatus, criteria, and any prior note. `update_goal` lets it report when\nit believes the goal is `complete` or `blocked` with evidence. The\nconstraints matter: the agent can read criteria and update progress, but\nit cannot create, pause, resume, clear, or replace goals. Those\nlifecycle actions stay user/system controlled so the model cannot\nsilently redefine or remove the user's objective.","tree":{"sha":"eb139f91aae8916962c5d2d1df2d2f5c0d69f052","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/eb139f91aae8916962c5d2d1df2d2f5c0d69f052"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/8fca61dc036888a4414ff5a4536b957c63dab4a5","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqQtOCCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAb60QAH9R8mEpWUc6pMMb3X+JRDJn\n8Y4p4isnPAm1CGMt9eQZstT5ZFySxkL51JBPveAoW2+BdGEvDOgcBpS8Kenc9J6x\nxMEWPC307FGwL0aEcZcxopCu+TORoYOYLUq2nfxZZSKQ0X0j+s9moxb2r4Dwng4L\nmXWV2PzbbkIQE3qnn2ey4lJCF18cwsn60HQtTHz+fBXeoDe5JTvFuVT/pXt7C6q6\ncW9++juA04XwdPil/qc2WzBItBzj/NfZP75LzvT/KhTnDShrPdt4FA0PFXNW+vvt\n7uqQibGxJvKJ3RquEcGWd3v7xmYUCQiKcZN4nLFYiQ2zmVvYQuybUAArTKrGDZ6F\nEMTXh/BepdXpSbZIHzqglM/MotgBCM4mu06Mey45oBTlT2SiA+ZbXIG3HASZsQtC\nWJfkqDTSQIjHLBffSOtcDE06gAvPvc5CjUsyrCXNed+7yWftYSTjbDBuLKXkXCPn\nDzbQERzAB/MyzL43IlmajNDUeTDMOUIwU+ZXpa3bcj1gW9yd1owGBGOG/d2v7Q3L\nI5gGBUYigrQ2Vc/cwLo7RJ4Us/iKscCwzp8FGtRaazoq1dWNBI+CVpTVyuXDaQVu\nCLfewFFST2SegF8tlx7mYlvbbefSCBihBwPZn+sjxMPDvn06hL1G6bb1At9XVicm\nUO6LjhqBol5wQRW8y3B0\n=y2AD\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree eb139f91aae8916962c5d2d1df2d2f5c0d69f052\nparent 4ab860f007832821bd303809d7c2c1d2c86a6528\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1782764418 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1782764418 -0400\n\nfeat(code): add rubric-backed goal workflow (#4365)\n\nAdds rubric-driven acceptance criteria to Deep Agents Code and layers a\ngoal workflow on top of it.\n\nA rubric is the explicit definition of done. Use it when you already\nknow the criteria the agent should satisfy before it considers the work\ncomplete. Criteria can be sticky for the thread, one-shot for the next\nturn, or loaded from a file. While the agent works, the TUI shows\ngrading lifecycle messages so the user can see when the work is being\nchecked, revised, satisfied, or stopped.\n\nUsage examples:\n\n```text\n/rubric set tests pass; no unrelated files changed; help text is updated\n/rubric next only change the auth callback; do not refactor unrelated code\n/rubric file acceptance.md\n/rubric show\n/rubric clear\n```\n\nA goal is the objective-oriented workflow. Use it when you know the\noutcome, but want `dcode` to propose acceptance criteria before\nexecution. `/goal <objective>` asks the model to draft criteria and\ndisplays them in an inline review prompt. The user can accept the\ncriteria, edit them directly, reject them with feedback to regenerate,\nor cancel. Accepted goal criteria become the sticky rubric for the\nthread.\n\nUsage examples:\n\n```text\n/goal add OAuth refresh handling\n/goal show\n/goal clear\n```\n\nThe `--goal` CLI flag starts the same goal-review workflow when\nlaunching the TUI. It is intentionally interactive: the generated\ncriteria must be reviewed before execution. After the user accepts the\nproposal, the accepted goal is sent as the first task.\n\n```bash\ndcode --goal \"add OAuth refresh handling\"\n```\n\n`--goal` cannot be combined with `-n`, `-m`, `--skill`, or `--rubric`.\nFor non-interactive/headless runs, users should provide criteria\nexplicitly with `--rubric` instead:\n\n```bash\ndcode -n \"implement OAuth refresh handling\" --rubric \"tests pass; no unrelated files changed\"\ndcode -n \"implement OAuth refresh handling\" --rubric @acceptance.md\n```\n\nAccepted goal/rubric state is persisted on the thread and restored on\nresume. For example, a user can set `/goal add OAuth refresh handling`,\naccept the proposed criteria, quit the TUI, and later resume the same\nthread with the goal and criteria still active. That matters because the\nacceptance criteria continue to guide future turns and remain visible in\n`/goal show` instead of becoming hidden context that disappears between\nsessions.\n\nWhen the agent believes the goal is done, it does not get to declare\nvictory on its own. For example, after implementing OAuth refresh\nhandling, the agent can ask to mark the goal complete with evidence such\nas \"tests pass.\" `dcode` keeps that request pending until the rubric\ncheck finishes. If the rubric still needs revision, the goal stays\nactive and the user sees why it was not completed. If the rubric is\nsatisfied, auto-approve mode records the completion automatically;\nmanual mode asks the user before changing the goal status. This keeps\nthe user's accepted criteria as the source of truth for whether the goal\nis actually finished.\n\nThe active criteria and goal are also visible to the agent through\nconstrained tools. `get_rubric` lets the agent inspect the current\ncriteria and whether they came from a goal, a sticky rubric, or the\ncurrent invocation. `get_goal` lets it inspect the active objective,\nstatus, criteria, and any prior note. `update_goal` lets it report when\nit believes the goal is `complete` or `blocked` with evidence. The\nconstraints matter: the agent can read criteria and update progress, but\nit cannot create, pause, resume, clear, or replace goals. Those\nlifecycle actions stay user/system controlled so the model cannot\nsilently redefine or remove the user's objective.","verified_at":"2026-06-29T20:20:19Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/8fca61dc036888a4414ff5a4536b957c63dab4a5","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/8fca61dc036888a4414ff5a4536b957c63dab4a5","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/8fca61dc036888a4414ff5a4536b957c63dab4a5/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"4ab860f007832821bd303809d7c2c1d2c86a6528","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/4ab860f007832821bd303809d7c2c1d2c86a6528","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/4ab860f007832821bd303809d7c2c1d2c86a6528"}]},{"sha":"4ab860f007832821bd303809d7c2c1d2c86a6528","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKDRhYjg2MGYwMDc4MzI4MjFiZDMwMzgwOWQ3YzJjMWQyYzg2YTY1Mjg","commit":{"author":{"name":"Hunter Lovell","email":"40191806+hntrl@users.noreply.github.com","date":"2026-06-29T19:52:46Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-29T19:52:46Z"},"message":"fix(quickjs): correct `eval` await description (#4371)\n\nCloses #4370\n\n`render_eval_tool_description` said top-level `await` would not resolve,\ncontradicting the REPL behavior and system prompt. This updates the\npublic `eval` tool description to state that top-level `await` is\nsupported and that final-expression Promises resolve before returning.\n\nAdded a prompt-rendering regression assertion for all persistence modes.\n\nMade by [Open\nSWE](https://openswe.vercel.app/agents/d035df94-2193-26d9-cc9c-942e81cc54e9)\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"a71d0b1e3d1eace572442c60cefdf7493fa1ddd1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/a71d0b1e3d1eace572442c60cefdf7493fa1ddd1"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/4ab860f007832821bd303809d7c2c1d2c86a6528","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqQs0OCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA86IQALCCKmqxDZZB0u5lDoXZjdwD\n8SSxYdO1tXvTc/fDY3dAl8r95Yj/NyarWUihfeXEexW07ZqJlsc+2PwzTtICZfIj\nYU5nemJyvmC6pPppsDGW5m9VgvwdhC3DaT14kNjqvYwk5j4FDjKhieEVEWIZPo6t\nSM7SHd5qin+k/6IGEQXi0fDG4ELoxhTXhw4ZpGcvcQscr38wMaQw8cOtrpv/pxCb\n1+7+TTiXmV4lZRRmtxSCFJc7Uo32OvKCv0C92R0rLSiONS/TkdqZbNZIcbcs9Opy\nddS9jlZnWH+h/w7jC18NC0DqXLYO+mcScvTXdkoE2KQsSkZQlL2l4VXWN7YcPVzN\nh12UHlIcxs8u1P4cpVPIGYtja4ku69QEY88Hi3MKurZDLg5fk9MfrvIZu8uDk9KJ\nCnBfo2jvhYsTpfaJMj1TFgFU52ei3gzgHzaw0JufSRhK0CItPvWH5cGDYFoe+GFH\n/Bdpi72dN3IK8Yzq35fzI0IbvWYs3C9u/oCVDN90XomkLttXIaMk6QE5QEuW39eA\na6iEaBteOzX4ObfF5t6tCQsV9LcU8v9sVrcjK7sgPnTMjQUL/+5DRNfsNhWg97K+\nmVYeJHUQuzy0Ea4+B//83tEBZBugd17qjhclII6rE5CkOEaNYmVUNnFwXIeO4XJ0\n4cJd3rNyuyi1RNOzGmSz\n=Od1z\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree a71d0b1e3d1eace572442c60cefdf7493fa1ddd1\nparent 5e01fec72d8b179a3b075b07268162d2eaebfe84\nauthor Hunter Lovell <40191806+hntrl@users.noreply.github.com> 1782762766 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1782762766 -0400\n\nfix(quickjs): correct `eval` await description (#4371)\n\nCloses #4370\n\n`render_eval_tool_description` said top-level `await` would not resolve,\ncontradicting the REPL behavior and system prompt. This updates the\npublic `eval` tool description to state that top-level `await` is\nsupported and that final-expression Promises resolve before returning.\n\nAdded a prompt-rendering regression assertion for all persistence modes.\n\nMade by [Open\nSWE](https://openswe.vercel.app/agents/d035df94-2193-26d9-cc9c-942e81cc54e9)\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","verified_at":"2026-06-29T19:52:46Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/4ab860f007832821bd303809d7c2c1d2c86a6528","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/4ab860f007832821bd303809d7c2c1d2c86a6528","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/4ab860f007832821bd303809d7c2c1d2c86a6528/comments","author":{"login":"hntrl","id":40191806,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQwMTkxODA2","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/40191806?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/hntrl","html_url":"https://github.com/hntrl","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hntrl/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hntrl/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hntrl/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hntrl/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hntrl/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hntrl/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hntrl/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hntrl/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hntrl/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"5e01fec72d8b179a3b075b07268162d2eaebfe84","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/5e01fec72d8b179a3b075b07268162d2eaebfe84","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/5e01fec72d8b179a3b075b07268162d2eaebfe84"}]},{"sha":"5e01fec72d8b179a3b075b07268162d2eaebfe84","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKDVlMDFmZWM3MmQ4YjE3OWEzYjA3NWIwNzI2ODE2MmQyZWFlYmZlODQ","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-06-29T05:21:19Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-29T05:21:19Z"},"message":"fix(code): redact LangSmith trace secrets by default (#4356)\n\n`dcode` now opts its LangSmith tracing client into the SDK secret\nanonymizer before agent traces are uploaded. Redaction defaults on, can\nbe disabled explicitly, and fails closed by turning tracing off if the\nredacting client cannot be installed.\n\n<img width=\"609\" height=\"95\" alt=\"Screenshot 5\"\nsrc=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/6a96f4d2-b115-41eb-9df0-ad8e7bf652c9\"\n/>\n\n<img width=\"1013\" height=\"390\" alt=\"Screenshot 8\"\nsrc=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/c9251d0d-f7a9-4251-b811-76be9d1d0beb\"\n/>\n\n## Changes\n- Add the `tracing.langsmith_redact` config option and\n`DEEPAGENTS_CODE_LANGSMITH_REDACT` env var, defaulting to enabled. This\ncontrols whether `dcode` installs the LangSmith SDK\n[`Client(anonymizer=...)`](https://docs.langchain.com/langsmith/mask-inputs-outputs#rule-based-masking-of-inputs-and-outputs)\noption with the curated\n[`create_secret_anonymizer()`](https://reference.langchain.com/python/langsmith/anonymizer/create_secret_anonymizer)\npreset.\n- In practice, users get secret redaction without changing their setup.\n- Users who need to opt out for controlled local debugging can set\n`DEEPAGENTS_CODE_LANGSMITH_REDACT=false` or the matching `config.toml`\nvalue.\n- Install a `Client(anonymizer=create_secret_anonymizer())` in the\nprocess that emits the main `dcode` agent traces.\n- `dcode` runs the terminal UI in one process and the agent graph in a\nLangGraph server subprocess.\n- The server subprocess is the important path for this rollout: it runs\nthe agent graph, so it emits the main LangSmith traces for model calls,\ntool calls, and agent turns.\n- The app process still configures the redacting client during bootstrap\nand `/auth` changes as a defensive consistency measure for any\nin-process SDK tracing, but that does not replace the server-side setup.\n- Treat redaction setup failures as fail-closed by disabling tracing\nrather than allowing unredacted trace uploads.\n- In practice, if `dcode` sees tracing is active but cannot create or\ninstall the redacting LangSmith client, it calls\n`langsmith.configure(enabled=False)`.\n- If even that fails, it clears the tracing-enable environment variables\nas a last-resort barrier.\n- The user loses tracing for that run instead of uploading prompts, tool\nI/O, shell commands, file contents, metadata, or model outputs without\nsecret redaction.\n- Preserve support for LangSmith profile credentials, custom endpoints,\nreplica tracing, and legacy `LANGCHAIN_API_KEY` while configuring the\nredacting client.\n- For example, a user with only `LANGSMITH_PROFILE` /\n`LANGSMITH_CONFIG_FILE` still gets a redacting client without forwarding\nan env API key.\n- For example, a local or self-hosted endpoint set with\n`LANGSMITH_ENDPOINT=http://localhost:1984` is passed through as\n`api_url` on the redacting client.\n- For example, `LANGSMITH_RUNS_ENDPOINTS` replica uploads also trigger\nredaction setup, even without a top-level API key.\n- For example,\n`DEEPAGENTS_CODE_LANGSMITH_REPLICA_PROJECTS=personal-traces` still\nroutes through the existing replica path; the primary client used for\nthe run is now redacting.\n- For example, environments that still provide `LANGCHAIN_API_KEY`\ninstead of `LANGSMITH_API_KEY` continue to configure tracing with that\nkey.\n- Cover the default, opt-out, keyless endpoint, profile-only,\nfail-closed, and server-startup paths in unit tests.\n  - Default: redaction resolves to enabled with no user setting.\n- Opt-out: `DEEPAGENTS_CODE_LANGSMITH_REDACT=false` and `[tracing]\nlangsmith_redact = false` skip client installation.\n- Keyless endpoint: tracing with a custom endpoint but no API key still\ninstalls an anonymizer.\n- Profile-only: profile credentials still install an anonymizer without\nan env key.\n- Fail-closed: setup errors disable tracing, and the fallback clears\ntracing env vars if SDK disable also fails.\n- Server-startup: the LangGraph server graph factory calls the redaction\nsetup before constructing the agent graph.","tree":{"sha":"cc9d07f5c3655ce53a6cd042f554adf8fe477168","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/cc9d07f5c3655ce53a6cd042f554adf8fe477168"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/5e01fec72d8b179a3b075b07268162d2eaebfe84","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqQgDPCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAF+0QAI9MhZuMLBtCuLfQSxF5hTON\nSG1pDWNpCojy5CC0sIGHQ2vYt1BgQp2kcP8sXht1YMiU8/Ng8HdBqjPdYX9T5mUO\n6efj27GbJzEtPK11OH4MfWpLeQSwrwaa8VzHAHHdj4XZ+UNL2Obof0+ZxJRjPkvp\nwXC/4MyL5vi0Dbjbmas+8CjC4ON8QOa0za90hyrC6Ij3qHmN73nAs/tfpdSWRWf2\nY6agqhtj/lSVq9P8zP1HvqmuKbaqaEC1/bC91ncOBLNvd5rPOFckK1ELLayAaylU\n4U0w4aKau4bYGwCi9bY71MzxSpyaApVvGtzdR6U0XzajoWe7s4qpPUT8LQJ6ACPl\nFuRm2kfd+oUvJiV5+XRsqD+KIWciwAlxOkN/7WGBJR/tzN1EFoi2f65mD6r2QKIJ\nppHR+C2DNtSPXX+o/t6FXjblzmMOJo8KeF05S8iOv/ExY2kiAqwOR3yEGQLz/Xf4\nVCiiOJONlHDW3OWvi6wf0bkRoPh1KN9JWn+ZY0pRutRnXEImGOGaf1zxu/rMzMsK\ncfyTqT1KijvAftg67rK2RZAcZmQl5Eq8dDYotCgbM+0fEKV2PTUjCCq92Luw+/zV\nN0Se8Ux+tlKEw53D8I13l4V+iUQqeH2g9LtlvZNzwTVBM4lvyTmSN6wBseCuj22o\nbsCfkBKVBySotC1vVJ2I\n=L2SP\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree cc9d07f5c3655ce53a6cd042f554adf8fe477168\nparent 92272baf2b0dea4f4c4568248c9e33c0a366b552\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1782710479 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1782710479 -0400\n\nfix(code): redact LangSmith trace secrets by default (#4356)\n\n`dcode` now opts its LangSmith tracing client into the SDK secret\nanonymizer before agent traces are uploaded. Redaction defaults on, can\nbe disabled explicitly, and fails closed by turning tracing off if the\nredacting client cannot be installed.\n\n<img width=\"609\" height=\"95\" alt=\"Screenshot 5\"\nsrc=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/6a96f4d2-b115-41eb-9df0-ad8e7bf652c9\"\n/>\n\n<img width=\"1013\" height=\"390\" alt=\"Screenshot 8\"\nsrc=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/c9251d0d-f7a9-4251-b811-76be9d1d0beb\"\n/>\n\n## Changes\n- Add the `tracing.langsmith_redact` config option and\n`DEEPAGENTS_CODE_LANGSMITH_REDACT` env var, defaulting to enabled. This\ncontrols whether `dcode` installs the LangSmith SDK\n[`Client(anonymizer=...)`](https://docs.langchain.com/langsmith/mask-inputs-outputs#rule-based-masking-of-inputs-and-outputs)\noption with the curated\n[`create_secret_anonymizer()`](https://reference.langchain.com/python/langsmith/anonymizer/create_secret_anonymizer)\npreset.\n- In practice, users get secret redaction without changing their setup.\n- Users who need to opt out for controlled local debugging can set\n`DEEPAGENTS_CODE_LANGSMITH_REDACT=false` or the matching `config.toml`\nvalue.\n- Install a `Client(anonymizer=create_secret_anonymizer())` in the\nprocess that emits the main `dcode` agent traces.\n- `dcode` runs the terminal UI in one process and the agent graph in a\nLangGraph server subprocess.\n- The server subprocess is the important path for this rollout: it runs\nthe agent graph, so it emits the main LangSmith traces for model calls,\ntool calls, and agent turns.\n- The app process still configures the redacting client during bootstrap\nand `/auth` changes as a defensive consistency measure for any\nin-process SDK tracing, but that does not replace the server-side setup.\n- Treat redaction setup failures as fail-closed by disabling tracing\nrather than allowing unredacted trace uploads.\n- In practice, if `dcode` sees tracing is active but cannot create or\ninstall the redacting LangSmith client, it calls\n`langsmith.configure(enabled=False)`.\n- If even that fails, it clears the tracing-enable environment variables\nas a last-resort barrier.\n- The user loses tracing for that run instead of uploading prompts, tool\nI/O, shell commands, file contents, metadata, or model outputs without\nsecret redaction.\n- Preserve support for LangSmith profile credentials, custom endpoints,\nreplica tracing, and legacy `LANGCHAIN_API_KEY` while configuring the\nredacting client.\n- For example, a user with only `LANGSMITH_PROFILE` /\n`LANGSMITH_CONFIG_FILE` still gets a redacting client without forwarding\nan env API key.\n- For example, a local or self-hosted endpoint set with\n`LANGSMITH_ENDPOINT=http://localhost:1984` is passed through as\n`api_url` on the redacting client.\n- For example, `LANGSMITH_RUNS_ENDPOINTS` replica uploads also trigger\nredaction setup, even without a top-level API key.\n- For example,\n`DEEPAGENTS_CODE_LANGSMITH_REPLICA_PROJECTS=personal-traces` still\nroutes through the existing replica path; the primary client used for\nthe run is now redacting.\n- For example, environments that still provide `LANGCHAIN_API_KEY`\ninstead of `LANGSMITH_API_KEY` continue to configure tracing with that\nkey.\n- Cover the default, opt-out, keyless endpoint, profile-only,\nfail-closed, and server-startup paths in unit tests.\n  - Default: redaction resolves to enabled with no user setting.\n- Opt-out: `DEEPAGENTS_CODE_LANGSMITH_REDACT=false` and `[tracing]\nlangsmith_redact = false` skip client installation.\n- Keyless endpoint: tracing with a custom endpoint but no API key still\ninstalls an anonymizer.\n- Profile-only: profile credentials still install an anonymizer without\nan env key.\n- Fail-closed: setup errors disable tracing, and the fallback clears\ntracing env vars if SDK disable also fails.\n- Server-startup: the LangGraph server graph factory calls the redaction\nsetup before constructing the agent graph.","verified_at":"2026-06-29T05:21:20Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/5e01fec72d8b179a3b075b07268162d2eaebfe84","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/5e01fec72d8b179a3b075b07268162d2eaebfe84","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/5e01fec72d8b179a3b075b07268162d2eaebfe84/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"92272baf2b0dea4f4c4568248c9e33c0a366b552","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/92272baf2b0dea4f4c4568248c9e33c0a366b552","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/92272baf2b0dea4f4c4568248c9e33c0a366b552"}]},{"sha":"92272baf2b0dea4f4c4568248c9e33c0a366b552","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKDkyMjcyYmFmMmIwZGVhNGY0YzQ1NjgyNDhjOWUzM2MwYTM2NmI1NTI","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-06-29T04:51:19Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-29T04:51:19Z"},"message":"hotfix(code): set Fireworks session affinity header (#4361)\n\nDeep Agents Code was passing the active thread ID through\n`x-multi-turn-session-id`, but Fireworks clarified that header is for RL\ntraining and not needed for prompt-cache routing. This hotfix now sets\n`x-session-affinity` directly from the active thread ID for Fireworks\nmodel calls, while preserving caller-provided affinity headers.\n\nThe focused configurable-model tests cover direct Fireworks calls, model\nswaps, async calls, existing headers, custom cache keys, and caller\nsettings immutability.","tree":{"sha":"509dc010e2b5db56300486c2ea6580f0e0202807","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/509dc010e2b5db56300486c2ea6580f0e0202807"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/92272baf2b0dea4f4c4568248c9e33c0a366b552","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqQfnHCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAKzwQACrN89zOZ6l+IZZKCm4pJ5We\nCYb9xM+YpSpP8sbDhJ5wFjAB1ykEUgCRvuhDFkk8TaCyJatu2HkPQ9LXz8nKZ6wf\nyLCJoqfGNVEKoT5XET1o3tYlnKVuCYYhrdXKByWK6XyVQ+tamwgUZ9iJkNtzVmJx\ne0/64tYEFgqG3F+wq9OE7u+O8RomUoI55NvmQCkmWPaYjfQ7EwPVWKoKrAfDSIen\n5jfgp3Sf3LhSoDc7+JsQbhcq5uTSAaFfUPUAFXweZXnA3wymwrwYX6gWyv7x8kEQ\nl2KLsr/ZaTLxkRTaZrR/rpHkir5NQU5IYR94E4bRqNvgAlJrGcGtk5clYZU3Ak5N\nb5EdyaUibrApn/o9fRrcz7ZOcEDN2eeKHh9Zzj8pWtiXTd/99r9QQJH/uRRayXlJ\nzY4uTYsb9Mn16c/GwxjQ5coQaSRvx/DsW+84WpwVVZwqL+64vol9QJElgjSaPBzL\nUd3+XKPihRQclbwR5SJm5Q0xivpui6Qcy869LBWPdAgtfqU4m3clO73u1sk1g4GP\n1YYKDd0bD6+Ha5cXO8BX0uzbrKZtoBkGIPZ0UREPcWv3rVO7SYn6VdRm6fDY3QP6\nCuvN2OdgZG4QvR9hskHdVtBpbpL8YjBdHqF4OdsUFbQ0lMwO0m0lTCboLKErN7hN\nya8fpWMLObeh1ddrwBhx\n=FIrV\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 509dc010e2b5db56300486c2ea6580f0e0202807\nparent 1bcb112ee78138eca9cb400c206ce198322aae32\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1782708679 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1782708679 -0400\n\nhotfix(code): set Fireworks session affinity header (#4361)\n\nDeep Agents Code was passing the active thread ID through\n`x-multi-turn-session-id`, but Fireworks clarified that header is for RL\ntraining and not needed for prompt-cache routing. This hotfix now sets\n`x-session-affinity` directly from the active thread ID for Fireworks\nmodel calls, while preserving caller-provided affinity headers.\n\nThe focused configurable-model tests cover direct Fireworks calls, model\nswaps, async calls, existing headers, custom cache keys, and caller\nsettings immutability.","verified_at":"2026-06-29T04:51:20Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/92272baf2b0dea4f4c4568248c9e33c0a366b552","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/92272baf2b0dea4f4c4568248c9e33c0a366b552","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/92272baf2b0dea4f4c4568248c9e33c0a366b552/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"1bcb112ee78138eca9cb400c206ce198322aae32","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/1bcb112ee78138eca9cb400c206ce198322aae32","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/1bcb112ee78138eca9cb400c206ce198322aae32"}]},{"sha":"1bcb112ee78138eca9cb400c206ce198322aae32","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKDFiY2IxMTJlZTc4MTM4ZWNhOWNiNDAwYzIwNmNlMTk4MzIyYWFlMzI","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-06-29T04:50:16Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-29T04:50:16Z"},"message":"feat(code): non-interactive rubric grading flags (#4305)\n\nWires `deepagents-code`'s headless (`-n`) path to the SDK's\n`RubricMiddleware` so a run can self-evaluate against caller-supplied\nacceptance criteria and loop until satisfied. This is the\nnon-interactive vertical slice of the rubric/\"acceptance criteria\"\nfeature; the interactive TUI `/rubric` command + status indicator are\nintentionally left as a follow-up.\n\nNew flags (all `-n`/piped-stdin only):\n* `--rubric TEXT|@PATH` accepts literal criteria, or reads criteria from\n`@path`. `@path` may be absolute, relative to the `dcode` process\nworking directory, or use `~` for the home directory.\n* `--rubric-model MODEL` defaults to the main agent model.\n* `--rubric-max-iterations N` controls grader iterations per attempt.\n\nThe rubric text is passed as graph `rubric` state; grader model +\nmax-iterations flow to the server subprocess via `ServerConfig`. Grader\nlifecycle events are surfaced by subscribing to the `custom` stream and\nrendering `rubric_evaluation_start/end` (⏳ grading / ✓ satisfied / ↻\nneeds revision / ⚠ max-iterations / failed), and the headless header\nshows `Rubric: active`.\n\n## Test Plan\n- [ ] `dcode -n \"implement X\" --rubric \"tests pass; minimal diff\"`\nagainst an SDK that ships `RubricMiddleware` loops the agent and renders\ngrading events\n- [ ] `--rubric @rubric.md` resolves file contents from a relative path;\nabsolute paths and `~`-expanded paths are also supported\n- [ ] `--rubric` without `-n` exits 2\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"45f9300dba0b5d75ecc6d90c04f85864cf9cd9b3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/45f9300dba0b5d75ecc6d90c04f85864cf9cd9b3"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/1bcb112ee78138eca9cb400c206ce198322aae32","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqQfmICRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAHeMQAAQ1XenOd8xVfNVuDc6/gwxi\nWJtRKiS2lgd1UfiaWJc7F39yfDixN2PfBG3uhJ2BgUptf/VwHc2dMkujx/HZ345S\n7f0n9at53npcun6P1dYdSF3xJdaA/G4vMR+K6T3yU1N47yXvmMT31ymOrLW7Vlrb\nlKYHl66X9zxswZdv9Vo4hVpuiUmPCzEmzHk2Bbj+EilTO/k98ml9d2dnsB6HLwRj\nenD+ICeG0FfAnY3ww0SquWpva+2rlSbC2gZ+39yWSkaYvdnJMPgdfGVkxJD1sj8a\noFiNC7Cmc9wbupdxOTn2U8Wa87BnQf5Z58kP9ofBpPIPCB6F7VHnaczlHVkHR4o1\n6uZKZO2VYMEKZjEe6A+30vD5n7EA+jlU9W2BghK8MunpFmtWyqLqIwTBAY611lMB\nGni7PpafboXEgDsCKeA750QbZAymVbHZKhi0jmHP2rTB+vaS86KJCOsNTfvthd+4\n7DHHYdnC4fu5Cr8FcbgYVAHFjKJ1/5gnNOZj2rWnGpgw1ouffcilhd4mWDHBIMTB\ns5XrvRNdahBmRzlXbVQi5Rxk0I01qzw/qNzfHjfJIpD6UHu6v9KQzrWDsAdaxCvf\ndx6fp41o5JQ0G7lRLBdyURhTlFMTf6PesIBRYfWUTzt2pSdBjS4t/w6lMisQlNP7\nUVqgv+2+auAC4iucgvRO\n=Zjzm\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 45f9300dba0b5d75ecc6d90c04f85864cf9cd9b3\nparent 90ebb1d68cb5942f07847f6dce48c14c7caef992\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1782708616 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1782708616 -0400\n\nfeat(code): non-interactive rubric grading flags (#4305)\n\nWires `deepagents-code`'s headless (`-n`) path to the SDK's\n`RubricMiddleware` so a run can self-evaluate against caller-supplied\nacceptance criteria and loop until satisfied. This is the\nnon-interactive vertical slice of the rubric/\"acceptance criteria\"\nfeature; the interactive TUI `/rubric` command + status indicator are\nintentionally left as a follow-up.\n\nNew flags (all `-n`/piped-stdin only):\n* `--rubric TEXT|@PATH` accepts literal criteria, or reads criteria from\n`@path`. `@path` may be absolute, relative to the `dcode` process\nworking directory, or use `~` for the home directory.\n* `--rubric-model MODEL` defaults to the main agent model.\n* `--rubric-max-iterations N` controls grader iterations per attempt.\n\nThe rubric text is passed as graph `rubric` state; grader model +\nmax-iterations flow to the server subprocess via `ServerConfig`. Grader\nlifecycle events are surfaced by subscribing to the `custom` stream and\nrendering `rubric_evaluation_start/end` (⏳ grading / ✓ satisfied / ↻\nneeds revision / ⚠ max-iterations / failed), and the headless header\nshows `Rubric: active`.\n\n## Test Plan\n- [ ] `dcode -n \"implement X\" --rubric \"tests pass; minimal diff\"`\nagainst an SDK that ships `RubricMiddleware` loops the agent and renders\ngrading events\n- [ ] `--rubric @rubric.md` resolves file contents from a relative path;\nabsolute paths and `~`-expanded paths are also supported\n- [ ] `--rubric` without `-n` exits 2\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","verified_at":"2026-06-29T04:50:17Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/1bcb112ee78138eca9cb400c206ce198322aae32","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/1bcb112ee78138eca9cb400c206ce198322aae32","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/1bcb112ee78138eca9cb400c206ce198322aae32/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"90ebb1d68cb5942f07847f6dce48c14c7caef992","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/90ebb1d68cb5942f07847f6dce48c14c7caef992","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/90ebb1d68cb5942f07847f6dce48c14c7caef992"}]},{"sha":"90ebb1d68cb5942f07847f6dce48c14c7caef992","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKDkwZWJiMWQ2OGNiNTk0MmYwNzg0N2Y2ZGNlNDhjMTRjN2NhZWY5OTI","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-06-29T04:25:26Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-29T04:25:26Z"},"message":"feat(code): add Fireworks session settings (#4360)\n\nFireworks-backed model calls now receive stable per-thread session\nidentity from Deep Agents Code runtime context.\n\n## Changes\n- Add `thread_id` to `CLIContext` so model-call middleware can see the\nactive LangGraph session without reading global config.\n- Inject Fireworks session settings from the thread ID, adding\n`prompt_cache_key` and `x-multi-turn-session-id` only when callers have\nnot already supplied equivalent values.\n- Preserve existing model settings and headers, including\ncase-insensitive handling for legacy Fireworks affinity headers and\nmalformed `extra_headers`.\n- Pass runtime context through non-interactive streaming and Textual\ntask execution so Fireworks session identity is available consistently.","tree":{"sha":"f233e2f0a82241bbf9f9bb885024a15a4abb56b5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/f233e2f0a82241bbf9f9bb885024a15a4abb56b5"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/90ebb1d68cb5942f07847f6dce48c14c7caef992","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqQfO2CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAiroQAKvl0Gu04V30lov0Vuu0eC2/\nfZvLh7/UzjIBZK5W2SGhDFZ8twVWMUv12bw5l0dankpZlsCE4422yuZhkzZJAIrz\nlJ6MKYmz1XWFSlywdVKyQOkDwc+6s7tXhIioIPUZCfIZx6FBgFhI9qTxJWzqqcUw\nU4fUJBfHPc9aSQb12DNsemMO8yfk3UW99Y5iQCQrOyQm0oAiaTfnrW0tWGXk1KAw\nrQ7t4d+InrKR50+UkkwP1AAmIUq9j2PWW52K6UTdrZxMVpFnpfsYT9BYOpyqSbO7\nQH/7W0JdlYyjsrpGhu0xKEGU4InUK+yPPVJFcvMxowtVy2H6R27exyV4JCrf6fnl\nbRuVH9eZf1lvmCAshj3alBKkxtIS278xnaEVV7NhNLWAEhT1BJsKaqc8/Kt1CnW4\nVybL8rtcqn8wH58WvWi4+1L7u0QAASc9WlNRrHdIS7YdvE77RLYm3K/YX0S1e29f\n9MOC6NGla1F/Rovyyjb+iEWCHuvz7wCxO7isDFukrwzSKaayoZJ3z4wzbmd6VSJO\nN+8uXZlnu1NRyZUseUyvs0Jnh+nhe42vaFu8iivhjIUXZyg/hpNigPl/Zp9dFbNx\nEbQik/rs91BO3orpvRl0K5nB3a17a8OfPTyhYcPdnvd4cUUFO50FIT2YVA/KkZYI\nVtQQQvnner64j1bRpua+\n=s+uE\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree f233e2f0a82241bbf9f9bb885024a15a4abb56b5\nparent 15ee384117ccd955f7481346dd92b7f4b007a60d\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1782707126 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1782707126 -0400\n\nfeat(code): add Fireworks session settings (#4360)\n\nFireworks-backed model calls now receive stable per-thread session\nidentity from Deep Agents Code runtime context.\n\n## Changes\n- Add `thread_id` to `CLIContext` so model-call middleware can see the\nactive LangGraph session without reading global config.\n- Inject Fireworks session settings from the thread ID, adding\n`prompt_cache_key` and `x-multi-turn-session-id` only when callers have\nnot already supplied equivalent values.\n- Preserve existing model settings and headers, including\ncase-insensitive handling for legacy Fireworks affinity headers and\nmalformed `extra_headers`.\n- Pass runtime context through non-interactive streaming and Textual\ntask execution so Fireworks session identity is available consistently.","verified_at":"2026-06-29T04:25:27Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/90ebb1d68cb5942f07847f6dce48c14c7caef992","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/90ebb1d68cb5942f07847f6dce48c14c7caef992","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/90ebb1d68cb5942f07847f6dce48c14c7caef992/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"15ee384117ccd955f7481346dd92b7f4b007a60d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/15ee384117ccd955f7481346dd92b7f4b007a60d","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/15ee384117ccd955f7481346dd92b7f4b007a60d"}]},{"sha":"15ee384117ccd955f7481346dd92b7f4b007a60d","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKDE1ZWUzODQxMTdjY2Q5NTVmNzQ4MTM0NmRkOTJiN2Y0YjAwN2E2MGQ","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-06-29T03:56:04Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-29T03:56:04Z"},"message":"fix(code): suppress expected MCP reauth logs (#4359)\n\nExpected MCP OAuth re-auth failures in non-interactive mode runs now\nproduce the Deep Agents login hint without also dumping noisy SDK\nwarning tracebacks. Transient refresh failures still stay visible so\nprovider outages are not mistaken for expired credentials.\n\n## Changes\n- Added a scoped OAuth log filter that suppresses only expected refresh\nfailures (`400`, `401`, `403`) and nested re-auth errors while the\nnon-interactive auth flow is delegating to the MCP SDK.\n- Wired `build_oauth_provider(interactive=False)` to enable that\nsuppression, while preserving the SDK diagnostics for interactive\nsessions.\n- Changed MCP tool discovery to log expected re-auth skips as concise\nwarnings with the full exception moved to debug logs, while keeping\nunexpected discovery failures at warning level with tracebacks.\n- Reformatted untrusted project MCP server warnings as a multiline list\nso multiple skipped servers are readable.","tree":{"sha":"0cb3f24e853255fcda3bff329ceef945652c9111","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/0cb3f24e853255fcda3bff329ceef945652c9111"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/15ee384117ccd955f7481346dd92b7f4b007a60d","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqQezUCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAutwQADpD0hmh/63oP/GODaNVzXjQ\nCYmt1eNQRCCkAIQjDb5c9hTuDUycmU22aqJcltA5opNk6PhnlLxXWPFA+mrNdTGE\neW7MxJTfnjRM+sbRI3mBqYfz9E4/L+Wfec9VM7exPFfNlWHyZE1uCcnl9GANS0sF\ngsQzRbs0kmPP7KsprYSUx22Rz6iBAiTyHghCHhuep73pvRRAqVOcUK6MCAfZmODU\nweaPlX3Yz5vaTiUe4IXAYMFqH+CtZJXWL1JsdS6zSZo6mSrBp0hCJBgWu5MAjkcL\nHtHp2Zb1O5pA43NDEnfZ8YhG0QWkDJCwq4GEEMFR3Se9VSPcdwLzn0qwPcLiHs/z\n+j2VWKSO1e+X2JZjIsKfYaYC2lUOoyocrxbfQw0qIsBCnBeg5CjScoLDfy2qB9G+\n24a9PX1Khw1YXhh8AcwwMjscHtM3UJiNQICeIEnnor4F+y3cSu0xjPpScGSNUM5X\nSDtJmrLcS7P2eMdYksYTAjk/JQyIsyi7dn6PoWjqQH9cQyoiFHdeBsxrf9pO4Z/0\nSuS9xsma5UTWJQuxs3UFFnQFmrIHFd+H3albjTQZMs2oOFHUfEQ43UxHvZbN8RRQ\ntmENPV+JoLarpjX5tgEn5aG8IglXenvVvx4amZQOzWUbxlteZaH9DvOpfQTmBggG\naN+hhmO/ssZKa490KAFS\n=8ibg\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 0cb3f24e853255fcda3bff329ceef945652c9111\nparent db441ed306a8e03fb68f2ae6a2c08523e248976d\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1782705364 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1782705364 -0400\n\nfix(code): suppress expected MCP reauth logs (#4359)\n\nExpected MCP OAuth re-auth failures in non-interactive mode runs now\nproduce the Deep Agents login hint without also dumping noisy SDK\nwarning tracebacks. Transient refresh failures still stay visible so\nprovider outages are not mistaken for expired credentials.\n\n## Changes\n- Added a scoped OAuth log filter that suppresses only expected refresh\nfailures (`400`, `401`, `403`) and nested re-auth errors while the\nnon-interactive auth flow is delegating to the MCP SDK.\n- Wired `build_oauth_provider(interactive=False)` to enable that\nsuppression, while preserving the SDK diagnostics for interactive\nsessions.\n- Changed MCP tool discovery to log expected re-auth skips as concise\nwarnings with the full exception moved to debug logs, while keeping\nunexpected discovery failures at warning level with tracebacks.\n- Reformatted untrusted project MCP server warnings as a multiline list\nso multiple skipped servers are readable.","verified_at":"2026-06-29T03:56:05Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/15ee384117ccd955f7481346dd92b7f4b007a60d","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/15ee384117ccd955f7481346dd92b7f4b007a60d","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/15ee384117ccd955f7481346dd92b7f4b007a60d/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"db441ed306a8e03fb68f2ae6a2c08523e248976d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/db441ed306a8e03fb68f2ae6a2c08523e248976d","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/db441ed306a8e03fb68f2ae6a2c08523e248976d"}]},{"sha":"db441ed306a8e03fb68f2ae6a2c08523e248976d","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKGRiNDQxZWQzMDZhOGUwM2ZiNjhmMmFlNmEyYzA4NTIzZTI0ODk3NmQ","commit":{"author":{"name":"John Kennedy","email":"65985482+jkennedyvz@users.noreply.github.com","date":"2026-06-28T23:47:07Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-28T23:47:07Z"},"message":"perf(code): speed up shutdown after Ctrl+C/Ctrl+D (#4351)\n\nInteractive shutdown could spend several seconds in serial teardown\nwaits after Ctrl+C/Ctrl+D. This tightens the `dcode` shutdown path by\nreducing the server SIGTERM wait (`_SHUTDOWN_TIMEOUT` 5s → 3s), sharing\na single checkpoint-existence query across both teardown hints (the\nLangSmith link and the `dcode -r` resume hint) instead of running it\ntwice, and giving the active agent worker a bounded cancellation window\nbefore the Textual app exits so an in-flight run can finish persisting\nits trace instead of being torn down mid-request.\n\nThe teardown query runs whenever the session owns a thread. An earlier\niteration skipped it when no model turn had completed (`request_count ==\n0`), but that proved unsafe: an interrupted first turn can persist a\ncheckpoint before any usage metadata is recorded, which would silently\ndrop the resume hint for a thread the user could still resume. Avoiding\nthe duplicate query keeps the teardown cost to one event-loop spin-up\nregardless.\n\nThe agent-worker handoff uses Textual's supported `Worker.wait()` API,\nwrapped in `asyncio.shield` so the bounded timeout cancels only the wait\nand never the worker's own cancellation handler.\n\nMade by [Open\nSWE](https://openswe.vercel.app/agents/a3ed8343-0530-8ee7-dec2-11da90162628)\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Deep Agent <agent@deepagents.dev>\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev>\nCo-authored-by: Mason Daugherty <github@mdrxy.com>","tree":{"sha":"2c7ed64f0c0cff29e12fe1866eb78ea5b8cd0bff","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/2c7ed64f0c0cff29e12fe1866eb78ea5b8cd0bff"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/db441ed306a8e03fb68f2ae6a2c08523e248976d","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqQbJ8CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA4i0QAIUrDJlrHm8zEzh4ZdO4bEdn\nG3L4L3SqsODe0C4wSl6zo8Qdb1ITS47Loe3lzTAe2R722eWTY/g0dX5r/fQTmktt\nyhu0puNb7nHOWCW3mjrJDF7r0MoLjhNLRwj3HB0k067Dr+XhTpuKDgVnixT2bVK3\ne55403B+QrvJb+QSV7w8zdDVaudFpohhZT4m9ASfy0kLBv4SFag1izKnCQ4whRKf\nyHKyRfrjP1Rs26mebvRvgzi7jiVHqpVf4wdkOAD6smkpdD5lRCjydd26g7Ji8NPT\nrQwRbaXwybv1zA44avGsMOnbHYTBiVqY5JBlAolZC4hnNtwFgSdE8XrswhjVLtTg\nx5GeGsR6ft323r4DZb4H6TY6GRV9Me1F9RiSlhA7uJYcsVBeYhygCAd1bk2cFiGb\nPDbEKBXZyKmYGjgS9I2tL3TBk+xxawjDpfB/zPklSMPsUv6iejr8+CL/bMzjhL2w\nBRbm74OSat+wnhvufMFH37DD4uzLDNnQQtzl18jg2vaUQ884uVX25Ff+uCM6zWaf\n0eE8TjLfANyMs2EUaw/AeS8LMfEXPKegvQbiDA3FH3hG9t4waN+QiNz/9HyXjH9g\nuKytV3F+uD3AAsUkdIA5uqB1MX7h0BYYD/sXsuzdJ7aNWNmpauVTCK7Gh95K7uMV\nlR0qHrW7c+6HArAHgPgp\n=X82x\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 2c7ed64f0c0cff29e12fe1866eb78ea5b8cd0bff\nparent aa22d6b6d5a49e4d6c3aa2d4932df75d14d65f78\nauthor John Kennedy <65985482+jkennedyvz@users.noreply.github.com> 1782690427 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1782690427 -0400\n\nperf(code): speed up shutdown after Ctrl+C/Ctrl+D (#4351)\n\nInteractive shutdown could spend several seconds in serial teardown\nwaits after Ctrl+C/Ctrl+D. This tightens the `dcode` shutdown path by\nreducing the server SIGTERM wait (`_SHUTDOWN_TIMEOUT` 5s → 3s), sharing\na single checkpoint-existence query across both teardown hints (the\nLangSmith link and the `dcode -r` resume hint) instead of running it\ntwice, and giving the active agent worker a bounded cancellation window\nbefore the Textual app exits so an in-flight run can finish persisting\nits trace instead of being torn down mid-request.\n\nThe teardown query runs whenever the session owns a thread. An earlier\niteration skipped it when no model turn had completed (`request_count ==\n0`), but that proved unsafe: an interrupted first turn can persist a\ncheckpoint before any usage metadata is recorded, which would silently\ndrop the resume hint for a thread the user could still resume. Avoiding\nthe duplicate query keeps the teardown cost to one event-loop spin-up\nregardless.\n\nThe agent-worker handoff uses Textual's supported `Worker.wait()` API,\nwrapped in `asyncio.shield` so the bounded timeout cancels only the wait\nand never the worker's own cancellation handler.\n\nMade by [Open\nSWE](https://openswe.vercel.app/agents/a3ed8343-0530-8ee7-dec2-11da90162628)\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Deep Agent <agent@deepagents.dev>\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev>\nCo-authored-by: Mason Daugherty <github@mdrxy.com>","verified_at":"2026-06-28T23:47:08Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/db441ed306a8e03fb68f2ae6a2c08523e248976d","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/db441ed306a8e03fb68f2ae6a2c08523e248976d","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/db441ed306a8e03fb68f2ae6a2c08523e248976d/comments","author":{"login":"jkennedyvz","id":65985482,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY1OTg1NDgy","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/65985482?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jkennedyvz","html_url":"https://github.com/jkennedyvz","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jkennedyvz/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jkennedyvz/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jkennedyvz/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jkennedyvz/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jkennedyvz/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jkennedyvz/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jkennedyvz/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jkennedyvz/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jkennedyvz/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"aa22d6b6d5a49e4d6c3aa2d4932df75d14d65f78","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/aa22d6b6d5a49e4d6c3aa2d4932df75d14d65f78","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/aa22d6b6d5a49e4d6c3aa2d4932df75d14d65f78"}]},{"sha":"aa22d6b6d5a49e4d6c3aa2d4932df75d14d65f78","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKGFhMjJkNmI2ZDVhNDllNGQ2YzNhYTJkNDkzMmRmNzVkMTRkNjVmNzg","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-06-28T23:46:44Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-28T23:46:44Z"},"message":"perf(code): background refresh for `@` file completion cache (#3911)\n\nCloses #1409\n\n`@` file-mention completion now refreshes in the background so newly\ncreated or deleted files appear without restarting or switching\ndirectories.\n\n---\n\n`@` file-mention completion already pre-warms its index on mount and\nre-warms on cwd switches, with the results cached for the session. The\nremaining gap was freshness: files created or deleted mid-session stayed\nstale until the next cwd switch.\n\nThis adds a periodic background refresh of the file-completion cache\n(every 30s). `FuzzyFileController.warm_cache` gains a keyword-only\n`force` flag so a refresh re-walks the project even when the cache is\nalready populated. The walk runs off the event loop in a worker thread\nand atomically swaps in the new list — the existing cache stays visible\nuntil the fresh one is ready, so typing is never blocked. The existing\ngeneration guard still drops results from a refresh that a cwd switch\nhas superseded.\n\nMade by [Open SWE](https://openswe.vercel.app)\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"ed2786274c99e006936a0b3684fdef8547c0e69d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/ed2786274c99e006936a0b3684fdef8547c0e69d"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/aa22d6b6d5a49e4d6c3aa2d4932df75d14d65f78","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqQbJkCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA//8QADHBAmdmqkeoZawZymwzkuY6\nw1IT6jfDqIVC+OCTxi+WpwbjNavGMJwFHOjwTJhrffBmkkAjMasfEjZhcHo6E0pz\nrFFw5OYp9iJlxRpjU2sv8jUw5TrYeU4LBrGQfPwb5DYLE2RgUcajxqPYMPxR02ua\nzQtTDMLhWkDU9wO0kLOHtjXvxVav1/gmsIrpHCOBCGukR7ocgG+n2xtaeUD9+b1u\nvmFHVCVUcXtG4EaeHnnj9PoYzCe+O7EBbjkY2szvOW6RtqkbV5AwNsuddfbNhoan\nc67NWeeb/B+Rax6igHEqapRQCbNnGEsmg3usq7MsvWCvQenAsAbSZ1IOJIOuGKdi\nyc4/+UulmunIGsbYK7ki+rmb/EBxuZ54Xhdpos4BKSq67bm5NacItFOK5WXIjrf8\nXga9gnO1rH9t1mv+e8kyq4jkzoGMkNLJb2xWd2xtOIJWW6orivmR5ehDbRgiDu/m\nVqx1lQ4U9dSoF3LNL9O+JI8cUJ7PbLGQ46BpEiPWmspo5MJK947021vNMnxWb3S9\nyJpop3ExHsGqcMiou5Kns7Mq+htrczoAYR495QYK9trkZTylydJuhLR1BtjWOAPp\nqar7O41bP2FnMT975ag4RuJGPALRFR1IfpWYKRV95Ry1/aeBPtBpq4mxyiivEIcy\n50akgnx1BBJkxASuJ82I\n=Pdmh\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree ed2786274c99e006936a0b3684fdef8547c0e69d\nparent 49b0cce6569995c03e743146109366c8a8cd10d9\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1782690404 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1782690404 -0400\n\nperf(code): background refresh for `@` file completion cache (#3911)\n\nCloses #1409\n\n`@` file-mention completion now refreshes in the background so newly\ncreated or deleted files appear without restarting or switching\ndirectories.\n\n---\n\n`@` file-mention completion already pre-warms its index on mount and\nre-warms on cwd switches, with the results cached for the session. The\nremaining gap was freshness: files created or deleted mid-session stayed\nstale until the next cwd switch.\n\nThis adds a periodic background refresh of the file-completion cache\n(every 30s). `FuzzyFileController.warm_cache` gains a keyword-only\n`force` flag so a refresh re-walks the project even when the cache is\nalready populated. The walk runs off the event loop in a worker thread\nand atomically swaps in the new list — the existing cache stays visible\nuntil the fresh one is ready, so typing is never blocked. The existing\ngeneration guard still drops results from a refresh that a cwd switch\nhas superseded.\n\nMade by [Open SWE](https://openswe.vercel.app)\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","verified_at":"2026-06-28T23:46:44Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/aa22d6b6d5a49e4d6c3aa2d4932df75d14d65f78","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/aa22d6b6d5a49e4d6c3aa2d4932df75d14d65f78","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/aa22d6b6d5a49e4d6c3aa2d4932df75d14d65f78/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"49b0cce6569995c03e743146109366c8a8cd10d9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/49b0cce6569995c03e743146109366c8a8cd10d9","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/49b0cce6569995c03e743146109366c8a8cd10d9"}]},{"sha":"49b0cce6569995c03e743146109366c8a8cd10d9","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKDQ5YjBjY2U2NTY5OTk1YzAzZTc0MzE0NjEwOTM2NmM4YThjZDEwZDk","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-06-28T23:46:24Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-28T23:46:24Z"},"message":"style(code): replace `/threads` sort checkbox with a sort dropdown (#3989)\n\nThe `/threads` picker now uses a \"Sort threads by:\" dropdown instead of\na sort checkbox.\n\n---\n\nThe \"Sort by Created At / Updated At\" checkbox in the `/threads`\nswitcher was unintuitive: a single checkbox toggling its own label gave\nno hint about the available options. This replaces it with a labeled\n\"Sort threads by:\" dropdown listing `Created At` and `Updated At`,\nmirroring the existing \"Show threads from:\" scope selector so both\nOptions-panel dropdowns look and behave consistently.\n\nThe scope-select containment plumbing (focus trapping while a menu is\nopen, Tab/Enter/Esc handling) is generalized to cover both dropdowns,\nand the now-unused sort-toggle code path is removed.\n\nMade by [Open SWE](https://openswe.vercel.app)\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"1b23c47663b0b4cc73e2ce92a1f1c63deecc5cb2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/1b23c47663b0b4cc73e2ce92a1f1c63deecc5cb2"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/49b0cce6569995c03e743146109366c8a8cd10d9","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqQbJQCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAkGUQAArLWG/3SF0F6gWKb6Aq1a8v\nmGI6Qxy8X27qaNauhwL7WjIJcBF7XBOLhnSOmKDUTMwd2CHXadS0Tikx+Ay5nw1j\nI+V9JsgmBwcrcYLNF9ToUfNQAhtS++CKDELPQGqHAtuVpSgRyKAw5XXlCVm3NPOj\nNQ3eBGf6M4dv3G2DT8ajiaIl/6qLjdtC2nafKcjzhe2rQA3MP1R3QVYq9bBBc/ag\nTshEkzdmkYPEaMb5YQV3qHUg9RQkEF7AH8axz3ZU2Vo5PONDKnyg9e1IVbXmD1R8\ngScnD+nMyOH0dJ63R3oHnskLDTquO6xBMd5L1YLA6Iklqwgi2oGac27Ccy/Bp0Xx\n//S6K0JYgD6ThxkIeLF2Fhjqw9xC0hrvWlveeLfuLM2wMw1z5ZxlJSiFEh7YxrTY\npIb5DYK6Dw+5oOXCZ+U5Ob24UWFiG0FtfA8bf9HW1tyItddQAYAtNAnlSVaoIT+4\nqi7pi18FCwN2GEKVcgbO9LuTkk/y6aGWtTSc23EJR6GYdkBIw/a6V9jU6keQkePY\nYF1nA1BwHRLTKLD9CKOS2NMwF7K2zYVA50JZSSFh8wjjMa7Ie6J9lAHdMsIWqlD9\ntPmBrm12rieaQiecYTmPkn7AXZ6DGb/pwYEo/13H8RiH5Z4MaAIV7xGjyZBRMymB\nObzElLmIUF6lwj1lF7B0\n=Hrvk\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 1b23c47663b0b4cc73e2ce92a1f1c63deecc5cb2\nparent b870b18750f65442009028a85a2ac18f1b06640c\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1782690384 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1782690384 -0400\n\nstyle(code): replace `/threads` sort checkbox with a sort dropdown (#3989)\n\nThe `/threads` picker now uses a \"Sort threads by:\" dropdown instead of\na sort checkbox.\n\n---\n\nThe \"Sort by Created At / Updated At\" checkbox in the `/threads`\nswitcher was unintuitive: a single checkbox toggling its own label gave\nno hint about the available options. This replaces it with a labeled\n\"Sort threads by:\" dropdown listing `Created At` and `Updated At`,\nmirroring the existing \"Show threads from:\" scope selector so both\nOptions-panel dropdowns look and behave consistently.\n\nThe scope-select containment plumbing (focus trapping while a menu is\nopen, Tab/Enter/Esc handling) is generalized to cover both dropdowns,\nand the now-unused sort-toggle code path is removed.\n\nMade by [Open SWE](https://openswe.vercel.app)\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","verified_at":"2026-06-28T23:46:24Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/49b0cce6569995c03e743146109366c8a8cd10d9","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/49b0cce6569995c03e743146109366c8a8cd10d9","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/49b0cce6569995c03e743146109366c8a8cd10d9/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"b870b18750f65442009028a85a2ac18f1b06640c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/b870b18750f65442009028a85a2ac18f1b06640c","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/b870b18750f65442009028a85a2ac18f1b06640c"}]},{"sha":"b870b18750f65442009028a85a2ac18f1b06640c","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKGI4NzBiMTg3NTBmNjU0NDIwMDkwMjhhODVhMmFjMThmMWIwNjY0MGM","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-06-28T23:00:28Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-28T23:00:28Z"},"message":"fix(code): clear transient update launch status (#4355)\n\nAfter a successful auto-update re-exec, the startup confirmation now\nreplaces the transient `Launching...` status with the stable completed\nupdate message instead of saying `Launched.`. That avoids implying a\nseparate launch milestone while preserving the terminal rewrite behavior\nafter restart.","tree":{"sha":"c2bfcfa981c9657d9e640347d6d45867a5f459c5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/c2bfcfa981c9657d9e640347d6d45867a5f459c5"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/b870b18750f65442009028a85a2ac18f1b06640c","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqQaeMCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA4AAQAK5dStZaMX7jH4EIpohBVKPj\nYZ/oiUYlHIVgdDVNdoCg7ljGCOo7HqoAjI//S51W4QOtUzSUbvy8oDBZ7Ro0eGCl\n5VPgpdsjDDCqJqStJu0LVemvOT8MmsulrngGRI9vZwmaJiNetiKLcS776zaop5vV\nBsnX6gQDlYkAVNW30nWM4PIXslBWAvpXYhJJ8Dv4RsAJfxsbCloIfQoyDDtLvhyU\nShvf3JUtTRiPEqs3FEwK7Gu7cri2N53eqrXcDvCEjJf89aBbh/VeYenjz/cpCrrZ\nwqYi4mERFt9muXmoesYOHaQjSrki4pJdo7UuVmnbSs8yywSiWdpMhacUtqq6rYp7\nRSLU5aWSU6HzKCa+3maBGgFeE7gxyEhz58/CILBXY/nGZK5u9ag3xHxWG0HR2pQH\ngKJO5Ca7ioj5VMeVuVxG18uOqA0Wz++biHWjm14dtPJurJSFywAtcUqsOI3a1vYp\nU5hmPIMj6f+0W5h+0QOC1BFmv8DcCjn7bCDaPZxmH5lbLy1jMBEXppegF3EYdWHC\nFH5neUyVla2zlNXJu3jZtNN/TNlfiV6Ucwh1/W2fwasluELic+Jw9ie7EOO0eUsz\nin1uKJANW2jbWvK8WGznnwNhZmJjkW0tEyiICJB7eCIsTAJMfUm2FLtSHkfviTQX\n1/MngAe84eZCklk8mM10\n=n/jb\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree c2bfcfa981c9657d9e640347d6d45867a5f459c5\nparent d7895c4f9b996ad6fe194936bbeaa8beea21e913\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1782687628 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1782687628 -0400\n\nfix(code): clear transient update launch status (#4355)\n\nAfter a successful auto-update re-exec, the startup confirmation now\nreplaces the transient `Launching...` status with the stable completed\nupdate message instead of saying `Launched.`. That avoids implying a\nseparate launch milestone while preserving the terminal rewrite behavior\nafter restart.","verified_at":"2026-06-28T23:00:29Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/b870b18750f65442009028a85a2ac18f1b06640c","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/b870b18750f65442009028a85a2ac18f1b06640c","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/b870b18750f65442009028a85a2ac18f1b06640c/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"d7895c4f9b996ad6fe194936bbeaa8beea21e913","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/d7895c4f9b996ad6fe194936bbeaa8beea21e913","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/d7895c4f9b996ad6fe194936bbeaa8beea21e913"}]},{"sha":"d7895c4f9b996ad6fe194936bbeaa8beea21e913","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKGQ3ODk1YzRmOWI5OTZhZDZmZTE5NDkzNmJiZWFhOGJlZWEyMWU5MTM","commit":{"author":{"name":"John Kennedy","email":"65985482+jkennedyvz@users.noreply.github.com","date":"2026-06-28T22:21:54Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-28T22:21:54Z"},"message":"feat(talon): audit reaction approval attempts (#4348)\n\nStacked on #4345.\n\nAdds host-side `tool_approval.reaction` audit events for reaction\napproval attempts. The event records provider, stable hashed channel\nconversation/prompt/sender references, emoji, decision, match status,\nand resolution mode. Raw provider IDs are included only when\n`DEEPAGENTS_TALON_APPROVAL_LOG_RAW_IDS=true`; raw provider metadata,\napproval prompt text, arbitrary message text, and tool arguments are not\nlogged. Matched reaction approvals use `operator_reaction` as the\nresolution so they can be distinguished from text approvals.\n\n## When this is useful\n\nReaction approvals are a one-tap action that's easy to fire off and easy\nto miss-context (wrong message, wrong channel, stale prompt). Without an\naudit trail there's no way to answer \"did someone try to approve that\ntool call, and why didn't it take?\" after the fact. These events let\noperators and security reviewers trace every reaction attempt — matched\nor ignored — back to a specific provider, conversation, prompt message,\nand sender, without leaking raw IDs or prompt/message contents by\ndefault. Distinguishing `operator_reaction` from text `approve`/`deny`\nalso makes it possible to monitor how often the reaction path is\nactually used versus the text fallback.\n\n## Example\n\nAn operator reacts 👍 to the approval prompt. The host emits a structured\n`tool_approval.reaction` event:\n\n```json\n{\n  \"event\": \"tool_approval.reaction\",\n  \"provider\": \"slack\",\n  \"channel_conversation_ref\": \"9f1c…a4e2\",\n  \"prompt_message_ref\": \"b7d3…0c91\",\n  \"reacting_sender_ref\": \"e2a8…77f0\",\n  \"emoji\": \"👍\",\n  \"decision\": \"approve\",\n  \"match_status\": \"matched\",\n  \"resolution\": \"operator_reaction\"\n}\n```\n\nConversation/prompt/sender references are stable hashes (via\n`stable_log_ref`), so the same IDs correlate across events without\nexposing the underlying Slack IDs. Ignored attempts are logged too, with\na precise `resolution` explaining why:\n\n- `no_pending_approval` — reaction arrived with no pending tool approval\n- `unsupported_emoji` — emoji wasn't 👍/👎\n- `missing_prompt_message_id` — channel didn't supply a prompt message\nid (falls back to text)\n- `provider_mismatch` / `conversation_mismatch` / `message_mismatch` —\nreaction didn't target the prompt that issued the request\n- `sender_missing` / `sender_mismatch` — reactor wasn't the initiating\noperator (when sender is known)\n\nFor debugging a specific incident, set\n`DEEPAGENTS_TALON_APPROVAL_LOG_RAW_IDS=true` to additionally include\n`raw_channel_conversation_id`, `raw_prompt_message_id`, and\n`raw_reacting_sender_id`. Sensitive values — provider metadata, approval\nprompt text, arbitrary message text, and tool arguments — are never\nlogged regardless of that flag.\n\nValidation run:\n- `uv run --group test pytest --disable-socket --allow-unix-socket\ntests/test_host.py --timeout 10`\n- `make lint_diff`\n- `make test`\n\nCo-authored-by: Deep Agent <agent@deepagents.dev>","tree":{"sha":"f1ce3761653b0310bebf01373052c910740683c5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/f1ce3761653b0310bebf01373052c910740683c5"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/d7895c4f9b996ad6fe194936bbeaa8beea21e913","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqQZ6CCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAACbwQAJRv5+O+a2jsRA3i1QEWD7Af\nFHgguzeQF+VQukEBjlqO13OScbN0W1lEQJ6jaXi5iHYC5ACQLq11Wujrl7ut9aWj\ng76S83exORnL3AzOa4g13ONzWYKFBTbz2kJdOZF3WMF3awsnTnlrtKsG5u6AGAEE\ntamwr7XZXfWLz5brocS+brns4wzuHvtjUXCAbJ+CADP5KtxpzOHiF//dPlUG+D+F\nWW4iBaeKMWiq3MJiHTGXoRyxlfCOoUs0SNnPtBBuuOZIzffOvEgwCAWVbGOewes3\nJuPvbQ2i9a48gzNJav76fXOfNZbsZ5kBA2o7am/nt1iIpPEVeSf/sSeMgyCjhAfV\nlKRabW+meltvGSLtGW7WkUyKlyoy04iegzoRtIKR476Zh5oPf/qHaWy0fuTdiGkz\npnJEp3pY9TFQjkPgeNTKcJmwtjiaFrOT9d4Mq3vuucTL6Xvts0L8/1MvCigBaRM9\nEgLN8lnE+mhZAgRFyZHRyAYvoIubSiG/YH4G66MR7Vsg7UZeUz3W39FhUCfhTarh\nJf/RApq5Ne3qp/oydUJCNIi06peAwOQSnY5BXNrclVRfA5gigiti4zwYWZFd2hLc\nf/9OYoCXdTvBsMiAZWY4su4VRgic+dtsrTKNouy0w3Typpl2xSidEw05bYsZhGxm\nm0ghkcXSZvmfh5KjhYV3\n=oxrl\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree f1ce3761653b0310bebf01373052c910740683c5\nparent 82d1eac59a43f096096e86849733aa716adb18fc\nauthor John Kennedy <65985482+jkennedyvz@users.noreply.github.com> 1782685314 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1782685314 -0700\n\nfeat(talon): audit reaction approval attempts (#4348)\n\nStacked on #4345.\n\nAdds host-side `tool_approval.reaction` audit events for reaction\napproval attempts. The event records provider, stable hashed channel\nconversation/prompt/sender references, emoji, decision, match status,\nand resolution mode. Raw provider IDs are included only when\n`DEEPAGENTS_TALON_APPROVAL_LOG_RAW_IDS=true`; raw provider metadata,\napproval prompt text, arbitrary message text, and tool arguments are not\nlogged. Matched reaction approvals use `operator_reaction` as the\nresolution so they can be distinguished from text approvals.\n\n## When this is useful\n\nReaction approvals are a one-tap action that's easy to fire off and easy\nto miss-context (wrong message, wrong channel, stale prompt). Without an\naudit trail there's no way to answer \"did someone try to approve that\ntool call, and why didn't it take?\" after the fact. These events let\noperators and security reviewers trace every reaction attempt — matched\nor ignored — back to a specific provider, conversation, prompt message,\nand sender, without leaking raw IDs or prompt/message contents by\ndefault. Distinguishing `operator_reaction` from text `approve`/`deny`\nalso makes it possible to monitor how often the reaction path is\nactually used versus the text fallback.\n\n## Example\n\nAn operator reacts 👍 to the approval prompt. The host emits a structured\n`tool_approval.reaction` event:\n\n```json\n{\n  \"event\": \"tool_approval.reaction\",\n  \"provider\": \"slack\",\n  \"channel_conversation_ref\": \"9f1c…a4e2\",\n  \"prompt_message_ref\": \"b7d3…0c91\",\n  \"reacting_sender_ref\": \"e2a8…77f0\",\n  \"emoji\": \"👍\",\n  \"decision\": \"approve\",\n  \"match_status\": \"matched\",\n  \"resolution\": \"operator_reaction\"\n}\n```\n\nConversation/prompt/sender references are stable hashes (via\n`stable_log_ref`), so the same IDs correlate across events without\nexposing the underlying Slack IDs. Ignored attempts are logged too, with\na precise `resolution` explaining why:\n\n- `no_pending_approval` — reaction arrived with no pending tool approval\n- `unsupported_emoji` — emoji wasn't 👍/👎\n- `missing_prompt_message_id` — channel didn't supply a prompt message\nid (falls back to text)\n- `provider_mismatch` / `conversation_mismatch` / `message_mismatch` —\nreaction didn't target the prompt that issued the request\n- `sender_missing` / `sender_mismatch` — reactor wasn't the initiating\noperator (when sender is known)\n\nFor debugging a specific incident, set\n`DEEPAGENTS_TALON_APPROVAL_LOG_RAW_IDS=true` to additionally include\n`raw_channel_conversation_id`, `raw_prompt_message_id`, and\n`raw_reacting_sender_id`. Sensitive values — provider metadata, approval\nprompt text, arbitrary message text, and tool arguments — are never\nlogged regardless of that flag.\n\nValidation run:\n- `uv run --group test pytest --disable-socket --allow-unix-socket\ntests/test_host.py --timeout 10`\n- `make lint_diff`\n- `make test`\n\nCo-authored-by: Deep Agent <agent@deepagents.dev>","verified_at":"2026-06-28T22:21:55Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/d7895c4f9b996ad6fe194936bbeaa8beea21e913","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/d7895c4f9b996ad6fe194936bbeaa8beea21e913","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/d7895c4f9b996ad6fe194936bbeaa8beea21e913/comments","author":{"login":"jkennedyvz","id":65985482,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY1OTg1NDgy","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/65985482?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jkennedyvz","html_url":"https://github.com/jkennedyvz","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jkennedyvz/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jkennedyvz/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jkennedyvz/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jkennedyvz/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jkennedyvz/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jkennedyvz/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jkennedyvz/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jkennedyvz/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jkennedyvz/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"82d1eac59a43f096096e86849733aa716adb18fc","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/82d1eac59a43f096096e86849733aa716adb18fc","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/82d1eac59a43f096096e86849733aa716adb18fc"}]},{"sha":"82d1eac59a43f096096e86849733aa716adb18fc","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKDgyZDFlYWM1OWE0M2YwOTYwOTZlODY4NDk3MzNhYTcxNmFkYjE4ZmM","commit":{"author":{"name":"John Kennedy","email":"65985482+jkennedyvz@users.noreply.github.com","date":"2026-06-28T22:21:30Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-28T22:21:30Z"},"message":"feat(talon): `DEEPAGENTS_TALON_RECURSION_LIMIT` env var (#4354)\n\nExposes `DEEPAGENTS_TALON_RECURSION_LIMIT` so operators can tune the\nper-invocation graph recursion limit from the environment without\nchanging code. When set, it overrides the caller-supplied\n`recursion_limit`; otherwise the existing default applies.\n\nThe default recursion limit bumps from `150` to `500` to match the new\ndocumented default in the env example, giving longer-running agents more\nheadroom before hitting the limit. Explicit `recursion_limit=` call\nsites are unaffected, and the env var takes precedence over both.\n\n---\n\n**Changes**\n\n- Adds `RECURSION_LIMIT_ENV_KEY` and `_recursion_limit_from_env` to\n`DeepAgentRuntime`, resolved in the constructor so an invalid value\nfails fast at construction (matching the existing `recursion_limit <= 0`\nguard).\n- Extracts the existing positive-int env parsing for\n`DEEPAGENTS_TALON_CONTEXT_SIZE` into a shared `_positive_int_from_env`\nhelper so both keys share the same validation and error messaging.\n- Bumps `DEFAULT_RECURSION_LIMIT` from `150` to `500`.\n- Adds `DEEPAGENTS_TALON_RECURSION_LIMIT=500` to the Talon env example.\n- Documents the variable in the package README.\n\n**API impact**\n\nThe `recursion_limit` constructor parameter is keyword-only and\nunchanged in position/name; only its default value moved from `150` to\n`500`. The env var takes precedence, then the explicit arg, then the\ndefault. No breaking signature changes.\n\n**Tests**\n\nUnit tests cover: default when env unset, env override,\nenv-beats-explicit-arg, and invalid-value rejection at construction.\nFull Talon suite passes (`178 passed`); the two pre-existing `ty`\ndiagnostics in `speech.py` are unrelated to this change.\n\nCo-authored-by: Deep Agent <agent@deepagents.dev>","tree":{"sha":"8483775a95b2723c2274748bce18ab62a19a1c94","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/8483775a95b2723c2274748bce18ab62a19a1c94"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/82d1eac59a43f096096e86849733aa716adb18fc","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqQZ5qCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAQS0QADTCMG4FywbkfrRdKBUUxjlR\noGjlAnYAMflDvnTstzgwzYExUKlQr8hFWpdRwnFrgeFhPmYhiA5+oK+KaqrbGpWU\nNmkGGcVRiLGo3vgLSTMcC73q7rswnMuhjoJzJIraf22q1Y2gSkkA4jFJbsRfcOSv\nTGWNWQylqXsNJKKOmybc35yPR6Y/aBtXC0XOx1NdRHS3NL3pTUllfdoUMocHA3hu\npwBu2diP2O15HGMNwc82lodTwNzNUQMhIQ5y1uMP9pxMEmGJsRWMGd8/dWZcD0a3\nvLm0Xy/CEw2Mi2JIckfKhz13foKTHaXYupwdan7ZHGT8Dx04yLsIOR1CATET3AzU\nl9MqhO2vL7U23OZjSSnQIBUYIYsjwnXQRY5t/CwAB3g6Gya0SnPWYClPq18sLws+\nqIE12Yc1qL4Sb7ilYJasCX7uY18KdYnK65CVqER5LtPwa4PNKZJ1FyvlQP+zVHXF\nEjK3JVJVFWe7XgSidjlbey3vL1neHN0AsPMx1KVw59FkjU81keH+2cDAVTDgJwRb\nV0dqAhPnZD1yUV8gy8uUwcduNSo8ctrWbVKPogKUwnQTga047lK+LjGYVg+jKWp2\n/HVNp8YHcJbcKCCP5BhkqOYxWrpj9SO7wp6B3ClVUx9BimV/rKaW+nGUyFiWIuAu\ngdbApCH1p8ZT/nnnpdAD\n=H+mH\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 8483775a95b2723c2274748bce18ab62a19a1c94\nparent 437af0bf79332b20ae0c1883c3cc4d91a98c2457\nauthor John Kennedy <65985482+jkennedyvz@users.noreply.github.com> 1782685290 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1782685290 -0700\n\nfeat(talon): `DEEPAGENTS_TALON_RECURSION_LIMIT` env var (#4354)\n\nExposes `DEEPAGENTS_TALON_RECURSION_LIMIT` so operators can tune the\nper-invocation graph recursion limit from the environment without\nchanging code. When set, it overrides the caller-supplied\n`recursion_limit`; otherwise the existing default applies.\n\nThe default recursion limit bumps from `150` to `500` to match the new\ndocumented default in the env example, giving longer-running agents more\nheadroom before hitting the limit. Explicit `recursion_limit=` call\nsites are unaffected, and the env var takes precedence over both.\n\n---\n\n**Changes**\n\n- Adds `RECURSION_LIMIT_ENV_KEY` and `_recursion_limit_from_env` to\n`DeepAgentRuntime`, resolved in the constructor so an invalid value\nfails fast at construction (matching the existing `recursion_limit <= 0`\nguard).\n- Extracts the existing positive-int env parsing for\n`DEEPAGENTS_TALON_CONTEXT_SIZE` into a shared `_positive_int_from_env`\nhelper so both keys share the same validation and error messaging.\n- Bumps `DEFAULT_RECURSION_LIMIT` from `150` to `500`.\n- Adds `DEEPAGENTS_TALON_RECURSION_LIMIT=500` to the Talon env example.\n- Documents the variable in the package README.\n\n**API impact**\n\nThe `recursion_limit` constructor parameter is keyword-only and\nunchanged in position/name; only its default value moved from `150` to\n`500`. The env var takes precedence, then the explicit arg, then the\ndefault. No breaking signature changes.\n\n**Tests**\n\nUnit tests cover: default when env unset, env override,\nenv-beats-explicit-arg, and invalid-value rejection at construction.\nFull Talon suite passes (`178 passed`); the two pre-existing `ty`\ndiagnostics in `speech.py` are unrelated to this change.\n\nCo-authored-by: Deep Agent <agent@deepagents.dev>","verified_at":"2026-06-28T22:21:31Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/82d1eac59a43f096096e86849733aa716adb18fc","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/82d1eac59a43f096096e86849733aa716adb18fc","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/82d1eac59a43f096096e86849733aa716adb18fc/comments","author":{"login":"jkennedyvz","id":65985482,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY1OTg1NDgy","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/65985482?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jkennedyvz","html_url":"https://github.com/jkennedyvz","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jkennedyvz/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jkennedyvz/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jkennedyvz/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jkennedyvz/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jkennedyvz/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jkennedyvz/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jkennedyvz/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jkennedyvz/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jkennedyvz/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"437af0bf79332b20ae0c1883c3cc4d91a98c2457","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/437af0bf79332b20ae0c1883c3cc4d91a98c2457","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/437af0bf79332b20ae0c1883c3cc4d91a98c2457"}]},{"sha":"437af0bf79332b20ae0c1883c3cc4d91a98c2457","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKDQzN2FmMGJmNzkzMzJiMjBhZTBjMTg4M2MzY2M0ZDkxYTk4YzI0NTc","commit":{"author":{"name":"John Kennedy","email":"65985482+jkennedyvz@users.noreply.github.com","date":"2026-06-28T22:19:33Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-28T22:19:33Z"},"message":"feat(talon): ingest Telegram approval reactions (#4346)\n\nStacked on #4345.\n\nAdds Telegram `message_reaction` ingestion for approval reactions. The\nadapter now requests `message_reaction` updates, extracts concrete-user\nemoji reactions into `ChannelReaction`, applies the existing Telegram\nexposure policy before dispatch, ignores anonymous or senderless\nreactions, and preserves offset advancement for processed or dropped\nreaction updates. Normal message and channel-post parsing remain\nunchanged.\n\n## Approving by reaction\n\nWhen a tool requires approval the host posts a prompt like:\n\n```\nTool approval required.\n1. `shell`\nArgs: `{\"cmd\": \"make deploy production\"}`\nReply `👍` / `approve` to run or `👎` / `deny` to skip.\n```\n\nThe operator can now respond two ways:\n\n- **Text reply** — `approve` / `deny` (unchanged).\n- **Emoji reaction** — tap 👍 on the prompt message to approve, 👎 to\nreject.\n\nReactions are gated the same way as messages: only operators in the\nexposure policy's `operator_ids` or the channel's `allowed_user_ids` are\nhonored, and the reaction must land on the exact approval prompt in the\nmatching conversation. Anonymous or senderless reactions are dropped. 👍\nmaps to `approve`, 👎 to `reject`; everything else is ignored.\n\nThis is most useful on mobile, where a single tap on the prompt beats\ntyping a reply, and for high-volume approval queues where the operator\nis triaging many tool calls quickly.\n\nValidation run:\n- `uv run --group test pytest --disable-socket --allow-unix-socket\ntests/channels/test_telegram.py --timeout 10`\n- `make lint_diff`\n- `make test`\n\n<img width=\"936\" height=\"738\" alt=\"Screenshot 2026-06-27 at 4 30 02 PM\"\nsrc=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/58756f30-c8ff-4bd8-8057-84c8681b6687\"\n/>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Deep Agent <agent@deepagents.dev>","tree":{"sha":"e350772de9f5f3c9c8f1c5b6b156e1cf08c4f2c1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/e350772de9f5f3c9c8f1c5b6b156e1cf08c4f2c1"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/437af0bf79332b20ae0c1883c3cc4d91a98c2457","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqQZ31CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAp4YQAFkXvAIy0Bmq8TahspaPNr1V\nz3WcXRt2SBQXekyHY78MJsNtX0eRPVa+wTrD4+DKgJti8jLFsKK/3XJXuczsleOm\nzti7sUakO9yvdnvXIbs5iBPHK0EbBMh5FQgjrVw7tEioSwTYuopqk2zUWBmXiLRy\nYoW8zPGHoUYhpu0T3YxMGCy2WdGJ9GrwalJ5YkXxIEAYcQpVkP3QP0AEowwdN+js\nTCEn0XWyKcgIjLo2rTe4Dg+H2XZFUlOF5hRtiyc6lHEiZJXlXk1IFYGaYVpkK5TZ\n7yuQIu/GjK1ga+yAgBI5VLKsjf9MwEl4ZjBnwmVl3qUe2M8uPOShxzxX+Vq0Bz5w\n788moZc8BrruI6/kuLV5W5trMuUSlcXba9cD4E6U4i82LwZVRWPKxCIPs4qV6p+Y\nIJtYCB17zksp3Ds6IgrWMeHqmM0/pvqLCTzgEmlp6Y0qSe1j+ekiAogbANqb1YjA\nDZP9zLgpFaNkB8X+SVJBqYAj/fuLJ99G8i3R6soRwNylvTsSVpv4x4gmKBkuawcg\nO6zXL+LT8nXi977S8QlrIGNR180L9lQZtSAei0QfuKiN84G9dGXBa458FjmSqArq\nmc8NZ3KPpCz2Yay5k5Rh/LulwUANvSxhWGNChnQijlynBybJM/am1mzcF/ewqVIE\ncscC5r+D/iI24FglWGjU\n=p8VG\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree e350772de9f5f3c9c8f1c5b6b156e1cf08c4f2c1\nparent d26481da615881bae4401dfa485ad925945e667a\nauthor John Kennedy <65985482+jkennedyvz@users.noreply.github.com> 1782685173 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1782685173 -0700\n\nfeat(talon): ingest Telegram approval reactions (#4346)\n\nStacked on #4345.\n\nAdds Telegram `message_reaction` ingestion for approval reactions. The\nadapter now requests `message_reaction` updates, extracts concrete-user\nemoji reactions into `ChannelReaction`, applies the existing Telegram\nexposure policy before dispatch, ignores anonymous or senderless\nreactions, and preserves offset advancement for processed or dropped\nreaction updates. Normal message and channel-post parsing remain\nunchanged.\n\n## Approving by reaction\n\nWhen a tool requires approval the host posts a prompt like:\n\n```\nTool approval required.\n1. `shell`\nArgs: `{\"cmd\": \"make deploy production\"}`\nReply `👍` / `approve` to run or `👎` / `deny` to skip.\n```\n\nThe operator can now respond two ways:\n\n- **Text reply** — `approve` / `deny` (unchanged).\n- **Emoji reaction** — tap 👍 on the prompt message to approve, 👎 to\nreject.\n\nReactions are gated the same way as messages: only operators in the\nexposure policy's `operator_ids` or the channel's `allowed_user_ids` are\nhonored, and the reaction must land on the exact approval prompt in the\nmatching conversation. Anonymous or senderless reactions are dropped. 👍\nmaps to `approve`, 👎 to `reject`; everything else is ignored.\n\nThis is most useful on mobile, where a single tap on the prompt beats\ntyping a reply, and for high-volume approval queues where the operator\nis triaging many tool calls quickly.\n\nValidation run:\n- `uv run --group test pytest --disable-socket --allow-unix-socket\ntests/channels/test_telegram.py --timeout 10`\n- `make lint_diff`\n- `make test`\n\n<img width=\"936\" height=\"738\" alt=\"Screenshot 2026-06-27 at 4 30 02 PM\"\nsrc=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/58756f30-c8ff-4bd8-8057-84c8681b6687\"\n/>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Deep Agent <agent@deepagents.dev>","verified_at":"2026-06-28T22:19:33Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/437af0bf79332b20ae0c1883c3cc4d91a98c2457","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/437af0bf79332b20ae0c1883c3cc4d91a98c2457","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/437af0bf79332b20ae0c1883c3cc4d91a98c2457/comments","author":{"login":"jkennedyvz","id":65985482,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY1OTg1NDgy","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/65985482?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jkennedyvz","html_url":"https://github.com/jkennedyvz","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jkennedyvz/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jkennedyvz/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jkennedyvz/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jkennedyvz/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jkennedyvz/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jkennedyvz/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jkennedyvz/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jkennedyvz/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jkennedyvz/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"d26481da615881bae4401dfa485ad925945e667a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/d26481da615881bae4401dfa485ad925945e667a","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/d26481da615881bae4401dfa485ad925945e667a"}]},{"sha":"d26481da615881bae4401dfa485ad925945e667a","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKGQyNjQ4MWRhNjE1ODgxYmFlNDQwMWRmYTQ4NWFkOTI1OTQ1ZTY2N2E","commit":{"author":{"name":"John Kennedy","email":"65985482+jkennedyvz@users.noreply.github.com","date":"2026-06-28T22:15:27Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-28T22:15:27Z"},"message":"feat(talon): add tool approval env override (#4349)\n\nStacked on #4345.\n\nAdds `DEEPAGENTS_TALON_INTERRUPT_ON_TOOLS` so Talon operators can force\nchannel approval for named tools at runtime without changing Fleet\nexports. The overlay is additive with imported Fleet `interrupt_on`\nconfig and is also applied on the non-Fleet MCP runtime path.\n\nThe env value is parsed as a comma-separated list, trims surrounding\nwhitespace, ignores empty entries, and maps each listed tool to the\ndefault `True` interrupt configuration. Fleet reloads reapply the same\noverlay.\n\n## When this is useful\n\nSome tools are safe to run autonomously in one deployment but risky in\nanother (e.g. `bash`, `execute`, `github_create_pr`). Rather than\nre-exporting a Fleet agent or editing `interrupt_on` in code every time\nthe risk profile changes, an operator can flip a single env var at\ndeploy/runtime to force those tools through Talon's channel approval\nflow. The override is additive, so Fleet-provided approvals keep working\nand the env list just layers extra guarded tools on top. This also\ncovers the non-Fleet (local/MCP) runtime path, which previously had no\nequivalent knob.\n\n## Example\n\nForce `bash` and `github_create_pr` to require channel approval:\n\n```bash\nDEEPAGENTS_TALON_INTERRUPT_ON_TOOLS=bash,execute,github_create_pr\n```\n\nWhitespace and empty entries are tolerated, so `\" bash, execute, ,\ngithub_create_pr \"` parses to the same three tools. When the agent then\ncalls `bash`, Talon posts an approval prompt in the channel:\n\n```\n🤖 Tool approval required.\n   1. bash(command=\"rm -rf /tmp/build\")\nReact 👍 to approve or 👎 to reject.\n```\n\nBecause this PR stacks on #4345, the operator can approve/deny by\nreacting with 👍/👎 on that exact prompt (scoped to provider,\nconversation, prompt message id, and sender) — or by typing\n`approve`/`deny` as before. With `fleet_tool` already configured via\nFleet, the merged `interrupt_on` becomes `{\"fleet_tool\": True, \"bash\":\nTrue, \"execute\": True, \"github_create_pr\": True}`, and Fleet reloads\nreapply the same overlay so the gate survives credential refreshes.\n\nTests cover the parser, Fleet merge behavior, Fleet reload components,\nnon-Fleet runtime wiring, empty env behavior, and graph construction.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Deep Agent <agent@deepagents.dev>","tree":{"sha":"b683542cb38a6cc197240d0b86e0d1fe2cea3fb6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/b683542cb38a6cc197240d0b86e0d1fe2cea3fb6"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/d26481da615881bae4401dfa485ad925945e667a","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqQZz/CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAtYAQAD0hLgE5SGelT+saiAP5DxVI\ny8pJm644urOPdm3tcygpljfdpe3w2Av8LEMTFfLIfXaVU++y1zDDZ1NUxBRYYLIZ\nrroe+spubZ2aKwxv5tWM+UiRUuS3dovVa+9HudyWFEYzUj0HgSOltQVDZzW2hzhw\n7WznQB6cSzg2ut3AahqbzlE7rV+0pScAaiXH3TIU166cJ3ZvpD8amTlq3y+82IBL\nLMuRqPiyaezGx/WJ+QKx/ZRtRp+fNUEDNHUOY4492jOrWy5oo99oWFwKSpcneSTS\nzB1BXAQ6gWTlJeoepA5uCKN323ZsDfb8JrxBGbudp2UraP6mhZ8bxNx5TwSktEvD\novimnL+bABijAAQZBVPQ0+6Zm94e0UhQY6yPpv4LmeaCx0+hYU31GcgMToItdTSa\nnQjPGYrTYzcRvuD0j7O3F0pkRQDnvpF4CQjtrthmoSKr8D0xR7/aeZt5eTuoItkI\nXefICyWHsIe6fVhlvixwe8Jp0pdoVjc2dhZ2HJi8gH2q9Q38V8l+3kgLHnZYkRIr\nfEJwgEpevl+hAr/aPFUN/zvykvJZuCKpPW7X74x4bleQS7g+Y4X4uXwEjZR/0tuk\nl0ZLAr3/6unSCIogP3L403SgUj9WbADjLH2GXaDrD6rWiZLIWz5jeezP/gYpUyT/\nvNEDZ1GGfj+4Lfxfe+Cg\n=KJma\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree b683542cb38a6cc197240d0b86e0d1fe2cea3fb6\nparent 3fe8c0c35536626f583df08573469506b9529706\nauthor John Kennedy <65985482+jkennedyvz@users.noreply.github.com> 1782684927 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1782684927 +0000\n\nfeat(talon): add tool approval env override (#4349)\n\nStacked on #4345.\n\nAdds `DEEPAGENTS_TALON_INTERRUPT_ON_TOOLS` so Talon operators can force\nchannel approval for named tools at runtime without changing Fleet\nexports. The overlay is additive with imported Fleet `interrupt_on`\nconfig and is also applied on the non-Fleet MCP runtime path.\n\nThe env value is parsed as a comma-separated list, trims surrounding\nwhitespace, ignores empty entries, and maps each listed tool to the\ndefault `True` interrupt configuration. Fleet reloads reapply the same\noverlay.\n\n## When this is useful\n\nSome tools are safe to run autonomously in one deployment but risky in\nanother (e.g. `bash`, `execute`, `github_create_pr`). Rather than\nre-exporting a Fleet agent or editing `interrupt_on` in code every time\nthe risk profile changes, an operator can flip a single env var at\ndeploy/runtime to force those tools through Talon's channel approval\nflow. The override is additive, so Fleet-provided approvals keep working\nand the env list just layers extra guarded tools on top. This also\ncovers the non-Fleet (local/MCP) runtime path, which previously had no\nequivalent knob.\n\n## Example\n\nForce `bash` and `github_create_pr` to require channel approval:\n\n```bash\nDEEPAGENTS_TALON_INTERRUPT_ON_TOOLS=bash,execute,github_create_pr\n```\n\nWhitespace and empty entries are tolerated, so `\" bash, execute, ,\ngithub_create_pr \"` parses to the same three tools. When the agent then\ncalls `bash`, Talon posts an approval prompt in the channel:\n\n```\n🤖 Tool approval required.\n   1. bash(command=\"rm -rf /tmp/build\")\nReact 👍 to approve or 👎 to reject.\n```\n\nBecause this PR stacks on #4345, the operator can approve/deny by\nreacting with 👍/👎 on that exact prompt (scoped to provider,\nconversation, prompt message id, and sender) — or by typing\n`approve`/`deny` as before. With `fleet_tool` already configured via\nFleet, the merged `interrupt_on` becomes `{\"fleet_tool\": True, \"bash\":\nTrue, \"execute\": True, \"github_create_pr\": True}`, and Fleet reloads\nreapply the same overlay so the gate survives credential refreshes.\n\nTests cover the parser, Fleet merge behavior, Fleet reload components,\nnon-Fleet runtime wiring, empty env behavior, and graph construction.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Deep Agent <agent@deepagents.dev>","verified_at":"2026-06-28T22:15:28Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/d26481da615881bae4401dfa485ad925945e667a","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/d26481da615881bae4401dfa485ad925945e667a","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/d26481da615881bae4401dfa485ad925945e667a/comments","author":{"login":"jkennedyvz","id":65985482,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY1OTg1NDgy","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/65985482?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jkennedyvz","html_url":"https://github.com/jkennedyvz","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jkennedyvz/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jkennedyvz/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jkennedyvz/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jkennedyvz/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jkennedyvz/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jkennedyvz/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jkennedyvz/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jkennedyvz/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jkennedyvz/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"3fe8c0c35536626f583df08573469506b9529706","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/3fe8c0c35536626f583df08573469506b9529706","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/3fe8c0c35536626f583df08573469506b9529706"}]},{"sha":"3fe8c0c35536626f583df08573469506b9529706","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKDNmZThjMGMzNTUzNjYyNmY1ODNkZjA4NTczNDY5NTA2Yjk1Mjk3MDY","commit":{"author":{"name":"John Kennedy","email":"65985482+jkennedyvz@users.noreply.github.com","date":"2026-06-28T22:12:54Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-28T22:12:54Z"},"message":"feat(talon): add reaction approval routing (#4345)\n\nAdds a provider-neutral `ChannelReaction` contract and optional reaction\nhandler registration surface for Talon channels. The host now binds\npending tool approvals to provider, channel conversation, agent\nconversation, prompt message id, and initiating sender before accepting\nthumbs-up or thumbs-down reactions. Reactions without prompt message ids\nfall back to the existing text approval flow, and existing text replies\nremain unchanged.\n\n## When this is useful\n\nChat platforms like Slack, Discord, or Teams let users react to a\nmessage with an emoji instead of typing a reply. Reaction approval lets\nan operator approve or deny a pending tool call with a single 👍/👎 on the\napproval prompt — no extra typing, and the reaction stays scoped to the\nexact message that asked for approval. This is especially handy in busy\nchannels where typed `approve`/`deny` replies are easy to miss or get\ncrossed with other conversation.\n\n## Example\n\nAn agent requests tool approval and the host posts the prompt (recording\nthe returned message id):\n\n```\n🤖 Tool approval required.\n   1. send_email(to=\"ops@example.com\", subject=\"Deploy complete\")\nReact 👍 to approve or 👎 to reject.\n```\n\nThe operator reacts to that prompt with 👍. Skin tones and variation\nselectors are normalized, so 👍🏽 and 👎️ work too. The host resolves the\nreaction to the pending approval only when **all** of the following line\nup:\n\n- the emoji is 👍 (approve) or 👎 (reject)\n- the channel/provider matches the one that issued the prompt\n- the reaction is on the same conversation and the exact prompt message\n- the reactor is the same sender who triggered the run (when the sender\nis known)\n\nIf anything doesn't match — wrong message, different sender, unrelated\nemoji — the reaction is ignored and the pending approval keeps waiting.\nChannels that don't expose message ids (or don't implement\n`ReactionChannelAdapter`) keep using the existing text `approve`/`deny`\nflow unchanged.\n\nValidation run:\n- `uv run --group test pytest --disable-socket --allow-unix-socket\ntests/test_host.py --timeout 10`\n- `make lint_diff`\n- `make test`\n\nCo-authored-by: Deep Agent <agent@deepagents.dev>","tree":{"sha":"d9c66fa545ab44f339591c03da0d37f7ab01552f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/d9c66fa545ab44f339591c03da0d37f7ab01552f"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/3fe8c0c35536626f583df08573469506b9529706","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqQZxmCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAO4YQAELwMpakd+QSnAq0NKZ9JY5N\n+UuPX6hQVCqjcqXYRBFYtmYXx6b12ayH4JZGVFUrAD8KQMxZvLMKQdIKtV7P+Ugv\ncFynQF2nB4QcoOitTBJWznjZZxdgfEzKqldJ4ogPadUmrhxMDybrknogzY4KcMz9\nGvl0gHe1+yeBYSVeygbCHBV6NR+vUxuPqdnVcXTpLSHpl0nSJBvB0Ymk1O3MSbhl\nxiKUTHjGdapVmdJdoA8nQ6kf/rZdlVRIBu5Ppa+8U6xEciZC9GG8guTfX0sTrka6\n3ms/h3TczkIEeKIZQvOBUrBmbOnG9C1c5AfymX+IZ8+acqcGzfdMebdC+3OkXsl2\nyXbt8Y41sEW6ejvb7XuYbjIOGIlR5au11m+2qaYdxovvBZccdBfo0l88JVlOvIjz\ng7SOkhAa5oZTQBC7JHlEIJB5n7xI+Vw9S8ytoiIISYwFqH7kpN9hb4Jz57bjQImy\n8JDuGPTf5vRwy+uINruHy51AXAFB/nRlOVO5tlB6rot3YBdVGgiPy48A6LDQSq2W\nfn56+Cn6zsdVDknBsLu+621CJwIG/FvKwMV9wneZWK2XIH6hLhQr/Y3NN3hGEAOp\nHHsBRwvxRFBW0Mhu40ljoFH2nhxG4xOdeSXkB3YQAPwPkDBfWOI9eu6qdwoxkcfz\njaN/9paKl80nkyadbwpY\n=I4fy\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree d9c66fa545ab44f339591c03da0d37f7ab01552f\nparent 0d504a5df8454e871597932ce1cd3e95b10ab00e\nauthor John Kennedy <65985482+jkennedyvz@users.noreply.github.com> 1782684774 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1782684774 -0700\n\nfeat(talon): add reaction approval routing (#4345)\n\nAdds a provider-neutral `ChannelReaction` contract and optional reaction\nhandler registration surface for Talon channels. The host now binds\npending tool approvals to provider, channel conversation, agent\nconversation, prompt message id, and initiating sender before accepting\nthumbs-up or thumbs-down reactions. Reactions without prompt message ids\nfall back to the existing text approval flow, and existing text replies\nremain unchanged.\n\n## When this is useful\n\nChat platforms like Slack, Discord, or Teams let users react to a\nmessage with an emoji instead of typing a reply. Reaction approval lets\nan operator approve or deny a pending tool call with a single 👍/👎 on the\napproval prompt — no extra typing, and the reaction stays scoped to the\nexact message that asked for approval. This is especially handy in busy\nchannels where typed `approve`/`deny` replies are easy to miss or get\ncrossed with other conversation.\n\n## Example\n\nAn agent requests tool approval and the host posts the prompt (recording\nthe returned message id):\n\n```\n🤖 Tool approval required.\n   1. send_email(to=\"ops@example.com\", subject=\"Deploy complete\")\nReact 👍 to approve or 👎 to reject.\n```\n\nThe operator reacts to that prompt with 👍. Skin tones and variation\nselectors are normalized, so 👍🏽 and 👎️ work too. The host resolves the\nreaction to the pending approval only when **all** of the following line\nup:\n\n- the emoji is 👍 (approve) or 👎 (reject)\n- the channel/provider matches the one that issued the prompt\n- the reaction is on the same conversation and the exact prompt message\n- the reactor is the same sender who triggered the run (when the sender\nis known)\n\nIf anything doesn't match — wrong message, different sender, unrelated\nemoji — the reaction is ignored and the pending approval keeps waiting.\nChannels that don't expose message ids (or don't implement\n`ReactionChannelAdapter`) keep using the existing text `approve`/`deny`\nflow unchanged.\n\nValidation run:\n- `uv run --group test pytest --disable-socket --allow-unix-socket\ntests/test_host.py --timeout 10`\n- `make lint_diff`\n- `make test`\n\nCo-authored-by: Deep Agent <agent@deepagents.dev>","verified_at":"2026-06-28T22:12:54Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/3fe8c0c35536626f583df08573469506b9529706","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/3fe8c0c35536626f583df08573469506b9529706","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/3fe8c0c35536626f583df08573469506b9529706/comments","author":{"login":"jkennedyvz","id":65985482,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY1OTg1NDgy","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/65985482?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jkennedyvz","html_url":"https://github.com/jkennedyvz","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jkennedyvz/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jkennedyvz/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jkennedyvz/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jkennedyvz/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jkennedyvz/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jkennedyvz/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jkennedyvz/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jkennedyvz/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jkennedyvz/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"0d504a5df8454e871597932ce1cd3e95b10ab00e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/0d504a5df8454e871597932ce1cd3e95b10ab00e","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/0d504a5df8454e871597932ce1cd3e95b10ab00e"}]},{"sha":"0d504a5df8454e871597932ce1cd3e95b10ab00e","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKDBkNTA0YTVkZjg0NTRlODcxNTk3OTMyY2UxY2QzZTk1YjEwYWIwMGU","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-06-28T21:00:49Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-28T21:00:49Z"},"message":"fix(code): record shell output as user context (#4353)\n\nLocal `!` commands are user-initiated environment context, not\nassistant-authored output. Before this change, dcode represented a\nnon-incognito shell command as a synthetic `HumanMessage`/`AIMessage`\npair:\n\n```text\nHuman: !git pull\nAI: ```text\nAlready up to date.\n```\n```\n\nThat made shell output look like something the model said, which is misleading in traces and can confuse downstream history consumers. This switches the model-visible record to a single structured user-context message, matching the pattern used by tools like Codex for user-entered shell commands:\n\n```text\nHuman: <user_shell_command>\n<command>\ngit pull\n</command>\n<result>\nExit code: 0\nOutput:\nAlready up to date.\n</result>\n</user_shell_command>\n```\n\nAgent-invoked shell tools can still use normal tool-call/tool-result semantics. This change is only for user-entered `!` commands that run outside the agent graph and are later flushed into the thread state before the next user turn.\n\n## Changes\n- Change `DeepAgentsApp._buffer_shell_for_model_context` to append one structured `HumanMessage` per `!` command instead of a `HumanMessage` command plus synthetic `AIMessage` output.\n- Include the command, exit status, and combined stdout/stderr in explicit XML-like sections so the model can distinguish user intent from environment output.\n- Record `Exit code: unknown` for interrupted/timeout paths where the subprocess has no return code.\n- Preserve the existing privacy and timing behavior: `!!` incognito commands and `--startup-cmd` output stay local-only, and non-incognito `!` output is still deferred until the next user send.\n- Update shell-context tests for successful output, nonzero exits, empty output, interrupted commands, timeout/OSError paths, flush ordering, and retained buffers.\n\n## Testing\n- `uv run --directory \"/Users/mdrxy/oss/deepagents/libs/code\" --group test pytest tests/unit_tests/test_app.py -k \"shell\"`\n- `uv run --directory \"/Users/mdrxy/oss/deepagents/libs/code\" ruff check deepagents_code/app.py tests/unit_tests/test_app.py`","tree":{"sha":"198c53f27b6c1cb215ebe0a39b23a39e4ef91d8c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/198c53f27b6c1cb215ebe0a39b23a39e4ef91d8c"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/0d504a5df8454e871597932ce1cd3e95b10ab00e","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqQYuBCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAmwEQAJfuJrU2WkcLrSFT4c+9IQMd\nZdO7A8Y2jFqyM62Nky/xpguPOH/uyUVet9F+wysxDKTkcV+WBOtslodS4NTiIDtr\nWnKsc+FM2R576vMYlx3hlgO2FN3dUxAeCvxrIx0QL2GUZHZp4fNF9OGQMkJEDa2b\nwosNBs9n/MNQ7seVLX8uXmdVmil3XmLecNsNEGtZ07mGJCaGSxAuYpYywdQXfSHa\nDYphl6wKFcpb5zaaget/x2nv3y8pa7KcH9JgRmRULeeeuk5sXjYc5fphBJnydpg7\nwrJk46aU9fM76Df8luX94Rtk9uNRvScnrf5F2pTcvXpIH6SnrF46y0X1OMtXje6g\n+l4jfVyHw48v3/MWLyiDCNlXCgfrc5Orggwa7W26DEifb+o/dbH2rF2gD7JUuyo2\noRtBqL0nOS4xC3c6KSV1kFUzBqESWljIPMGl77e6mno8HD5fxz7d9W2KowDdpmMY\niDO6KAVr5OnTwxeKwZPmv6t5+JaSDaktHxSrv2PrkntjsdkWsNcHs5AXqONxM3hG\nHUBnW/JFYeuHXKUv2QaxYcr0Vag6MuLMialrMDJtgvHwQmKzRcZmUTlx9M75avaw\nDhsXs4SfiVoXA5dnIUgzwsfMp0cXAPupnrmEOfr/wjwfEwswvMX0PZsl4/qEoVsi\nqKbl35CyY+hiff0IzxIz\n=SIom\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 198c53f27b6c1cb215ebe0a39b23a39e4ef91d8c\nparent 8c7ff17bfd48c9d7b922494b8c37aa14a7c25e8f\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1782680449 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1782680449 -0400\n\nfix(code): record shell output as user context (#4353)\n\nLocal `!` commands are user-initiated environment context, not\nassistant-authored output. Before this change, dcode represented a\nnon-incognito shell command as a synthetic `HumanMessage`/`AIMessage`\npair:\n\n```text\nHuman: !git pull\nAI: ```text\nAlready up to date.\n```\n```\n\nThat made shell output look like something the model said, which is misleading in traces and can confuse downstream history consumers. This switches the model-visible record to a single structured user-context message, matching the pattern used by tools like Codex for user-entered shell commands:\n\n```text\nHuman: <user_shell_command>\n<command>\ngit pull\n</command>\n<result>\nExit code: 0\nOutput:\nAlready up to date.\n</result>\n</user_shell_command>\n```\n\nAgent-invoked shell tools can still use normal tool-call/tool-result semantics. This change is only for user-entered `!` commands that run outside the agent graph and are later flushed into the thread state before the next user turn.\n\n## Changes\n- Change `DeepAgentsApp._buffer_shell_for_model_context` to append one structured `HumanMessage` per `!` command instead of a `HumanMessage` command plus synthetic `AIMessage` output.\n- Include the command, exit status, and combined stdout/stderr in explicit XML-like sections so the model can distinguish user intent from environment output.\n- Record `Exit code: unknown` for interrupted/timeout paths where the subprocess has no return code.\n- Preserve the existing privacy and timing behavior: `!!` incognito commands and `--startup-cmd` output stay local-only, and non-incognito `!` output is still deferred until the next user send.\n- Update shell-context tests for successful output, nonzero exits, empty output, interrupted commands, timeout/OSError paths, flush ordering, and retained buffers.\n\n## Testing\n- `uv run --directory \"/Users/mdrxy/oss/deepagents/libs/code\" --group test pytest tests/unit_tests/test_app.py -k \"shell\"`\n- `uv run --directory \"/Users/mdrxy/oss/deepagents/libs/code\" ruff check deepagents_code/app.py tests/unit_tests/test_app.py`","verified_at":"2026-06-28T21:00:49Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/0d504a5df8454e871597932ce1cd3e95b10ab00e","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/0d504a5df8454e871597932ce1cd3e95b10ab00e","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/0d504a5df8454e871597932ce1cd3e95b10ab00e/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"8c7ff17bfd48c9d7b922494b8c37aa14a7c25e8f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/8c7ff17bfd48c9d7b922494b8c37aa14a7c25e8f","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/8c7ff17bfd48c9d7b922494b8c37aa14a7c25e8f"}]},{"sha":"8c7ff17bfd48c9d7b922494b8c37aa14a7c25e8f","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKDhjN2ZmMTdiZmQ0OGM5ZDdiOTIyNDk0YjhjMzdhYTE0YTdjMjVlOGY","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-06-28T20:44:25Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-28T20:44:25Z"},"message":"style(code): use text fences for raw CLI output (#4352)\n\nCloses #1411\n\n---\n\nRaw CLI output and inline mentioned-file embeds are displayed as\nMarkdown fences. Bare fences let Textual guess a lexer, which can\nproduce misleading syntax highlighting for arbitrary shell output or raw\nfile snippets; pinning these blocks to `text` keeps them rendered as\nplain output.\n\n## Changes\n\n- Wrap local `!` shell output, including buffered model-context\nmessages, in explicit `text` fenced blocks.\n- Wrap `_read_mentioned_file` inline file snippets in explicit `text`\nfenced blocks.\n- Add focused coverage for shell output rendering and mentioned-file\nembedding so these paths keep using plain-text fences.","tree":{"sha":"030b1afc96ee7499833a3a9ee775ce00b8378ec1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/030b1afc96ee7499833a3a9ee775ce00b8378ec1"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/8c7ff17bfd48c9d7b922494b8c37aa14a7c25e8f","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqQYepCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAg4MQAFGp3gKUQR8rLUnMR5rN9FXa\nDyTFF2+oOFCKSx/S1gNGkvYS4qu+CqLc+JFOxiI3AYQu9oc7IRQz79nQEQhQkOws\nH7qUHJoE9q1I3YvHGDt9fWPJae9AGf6gCk24T00WdmQUYdA1wfjaF+NzpFtVAXwE\nc5pPWdHo8gBlLrbzjAcrsz/P7G27vk2tn2VzKhI7fcFOPrjT1bhQ8Nwy27xI5F6C\nsJ41XzIl39fUsENeayrmCBYXrlsbjKBaKVgIdg4LHj5+fLE2noUXXKe9tUrjy2eY\ncZWhn3O+oE1rArIgY57G/Rl3+3v6g/QE4d4fnhysTOYdaSn+C3XTU4vprmL+b0Mv\nLb/XL5H/I8PtXwvZLTLnBjtN/EBt4pmIkdbJPm2ftdRiLT5AP+TluBySogKYMTTW\nohbmV56SetlJJNE6mJWSOvLJMl+XzyPpwR1G8eBZPp90lBl1keb6olaDKU5VBXEO\nGmN9n9baD+2bXLLJSXwHGfuM1meWRSZ+GHxhN0K4XdRmpLJ2pBrGzbeK3nCu3A2h\nAZUl/tIwEXXh/u/IYvJKxST2gqqoAen5LLODtIDpozsvEvXC21RFRg9ou1PPL5Xb\nD7noPXfApk9WHabkqT8IhO6LvBTI6SXfQFzs3bQvkLXcrxkcQvgiF7p+tfYks82h\nDCOPeLg9jz9n/LnQUHoV\n=kiK6\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 030b1afc96ee7499833a3a9ee775ce00b8378ec1\nparent 863f311a31dad50c1173754baa7b7e430c197d38\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1782679465 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1782679465 -0400\n\nstyle(code): use text fences for raw CLI output (#4352)\n\nCloses #1411\n\n---\n\nRaw CLI output and inline mentioned-file embeds are displayed as\nMarkdown fences. Bare fences let Textual guess a lexer, which can\nproduce misleading syntax highlighting for arbitrary shell output or raw\nfile snippets; pinning these blocks to `text` keeps them rendered as\nplain output.\n\n## Changes\n\n- Wrap local `!` shell output, including buffered model-context\nmessages, in explicit `text` fenced blocks.\n- Wrap `_read_mentioned_file` inline file snippets in explicit `text`\nfenced blocks.\n- Add focused coverage for shell output rendering and mentioned-file\nembedding so these paths keep using plain-text fences.","verified_at":"2026-06-28T20:44:25Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/8c7ff17bfd48c9d7b922494b8c37aa14a7c25e8f","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/8c7ff17bfd48c9d7b922494b8c37aa14a7c25e8f","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/8c7ff17bfd48c9d7b922494b8c37aa14a7c25e8f/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"863f311a31dad50c1173754baa7b7e430c197d38","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/863f311a31dad50c1173754baa7b7e430c197d38","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/863f311a31dad50c1173754baa7b7e430c197d38"}]},{"sha":"863f311a31dad50c1173754baa7b7e430c197d38","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKDg2M2YzMTFhMzFkYWQ1MGMxMTczNzU0YmFhN2I3ZTQzMGMxOTdkMzg","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-06-28T20:39:24Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-28T20:39:24Z"},"message":"style(code): don't render empty box for empty file-op tool output (#3992)\n\nEmpty `glob`/`grep`/`ls` results no longer render an empty, clickable\noutput box in the chat UI.\n\n---\n\n`glob`/`grep`/`ls` serialize an empty successful result as the literal\n`\"[]\"`, which formats to no visible content. The raw output is truthy,\nso the existing empty-output guard didn't fire and an empty preview row\nrendered — an empty box with a misleading expand affordance. Now\n`_update_output_display` hides all output rows when the formatted result\nis empty.\n\nMade by [Open SWE](https://openswe.vercel.app)\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"87961b2c949c14ff0fc44d964535f81ed83dce79","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/87961b2c949c14ff0fc44d964535f81ed83dce79"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/863f311a31dad50c1173754baa7b7e430c197d38","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqQYZ8CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAB0UQAAhBZM+gLu0KUIwjIdkfWCRz\ndtavDfEol+qapxlxxooqSPsvrOEskxpIxQY0rSqD9N85hJe6vCF7IMIjr0LkHwa9\nvr5t44fgtdpNDrMsdS9jF5SOJWN5OmxC6jNsWHUM+HYuFAhOe+gk/dVTBMMWF+ky\nCefmC/Z4R/8LOu+dLGFFH/FQkSpvaUq2RzOoOpIfn8WQx/sKSbnKlvcR/ROp3694\n3PF6uEVN73dLAlrfMM96xxW/WTdrzEOH235Esm3MNX8CfFpJ+JVmQPks6e2huhxe\nTLgty4D6Jg7OnxR8Y6i7JHAgf3LIRRIX91d25tgZC1Ns2mnQl62Zo/O9unf87RFi\nQ/VG39xKNtGHIWbOyezeJ7nx5j9Esj/QociR6Y/JlyQgzc/yReWqJEr2SJ3SrdVt\nOEH3HzRW0msuFOTtlyOVVKmmA/Qcr/LMmQ/fHAsjailrbCjLQK6eirHu/s9pA4Wi\nqOLjCP653hS3L74iQb/S8n29p/3qMp9d/OPVCA6RfHSvbpeCAdrB6zvzrmat2WtX\nKH+zm98pFHtMsJIC+3vcsI4KWWI7ndCOg/dhE7amlO2WBBTu0ezchb+Te7njjrHQ\n2nl2l78HsyaRvTbfzykzbFFUDMIFJdu4ZzHOjKuA9Aw2tD2p14mv9aqNg94lNoDc\n8Pwg0+bIOgohRtvwSs8E\n=SmQe\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 87961b2c949c14ff0fc44d964535f81ed83dce79\nparent 02f5bd7bc02f2baaf5a1eefce7d686ba62493647\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1782679164 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1782679164 -0400\n\nstyle(code): don't render empty box for empty file-op tool output (#3992)\n\nEmpty `glob`/`grep`/`ls` results no longer render an empty, clickable\noutput box in the chat UI.\n\n---\n\n`glob`/`grep`/`ls` serialize an empty successful result as the literal\n`\"[]\"`, which formats to no visible content. The raw output is truthy,\nso the existing empty-output guard didn't fire and an empty preview row\nrendered — an empty box with a misleading expand affordance. Now\n`_update_output_display` hides all output rows when the formatted result\nis empty.\n\nMade by [Open SWE](https://openswe.vercel.app)\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","verified_at":"2026-06-28T20:39:25Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/863f311a31dad50c1173754baa7b7e430c197d38","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/863f311a31dad50c1173754baa7b7e430c197d38","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/863f311a31dad50c1173754baa7b7e430c197d38/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://gith